  <releases>
    <release version="1.8.19" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.19 resolves Windows font rendering limitations by introducing native scalable vector symbolic icons for article view counts and import actions, makes the Wikipedia Top 25 Trending Topics pane open by default for immediate discovery, equips the Windows multi-part setup installer with automatic slice detection and seamless background downloading for both Part 1 and Part 2 data files, removes obsolete Wikipedia importer documentation entries, publishes formal automated test metrics and quality verification summaries, and frees over 36 GB of disk storage by cleaning historical build artifacts.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Raw Unicode Emoji Glyphs in Trending View Counts &amp; Import Buttons (👁 and 📥): Removed raw Unicode emoji text characters in Pango labels and buttons in src/window.py. Reason: Standard desktop system fonts on Microsoft Windows (e.g. Segoe UI) lack native color emoji tables, causing Pango to render missing character hex fallback boxes (01F441 and 01F4E5); replaced with crisp, theme-adaptive vector SVG icons.</li>
          <li>Manual Expansion Prerequisite for Wikipedia Trending: Removed the requirement for users to manually click "Trending Topics (Top 25) ▶" before viewing popular articles in src/window.py. Reason: Opening the trending pane automatically upon dialog launch eliminates friction and provides instant topic discovery.</li>
          <li>Obsolete Wikipedia Importer Documentation Entries: Removed documentation for "1. Direct Wikipedia Article Importer" and "4. Non-Blocking Asynchronous Fetching HUD" from README.md and renumbered remaining features sequentially. Reason: Streamlines user-facing documentation to reflect active features without redundant or unneeded sub-entries.</li>
          <li>Historical Release Binaries and Staging Artifacts (36 GB): Removed historical binary build outputs from previous releases (dist/) and intermediate staging build directories (build-appimage/, build-arm64/, build-dir/, .pytest_cache/). Reason: Reclaimed over 36 GB of local drive storage while preserving essential build cache (.flatpak-builder) and relying on GitHub Releases for permanent package hosting.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Vector Eye Symbolic Icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.eye-symbolic.svg): Designed and bundled a native 16x16 vector SVG eye icon into the GResource bundle (src/readaloud.gresource.xml and src/icons/). Reason: Guarantees crisp, theme-adaptive (fill="currentColor") view count rendering across Windows, Linux, and macOS without font tofu boxes or missing glyphs.</li>
          <li>Inbox Tray Import Symbolic Icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.import-symbolic.svg): Designed and bundled a custom 16x16 vector inbox tray import icon matching the universal 📥 glyph into the GResource bundle. Reason: Provides a dedicated, theme-aware visual icon for one-click downloading and importing of trending articles with interactive #f6d32d highlight hover feedback.</li>
          <li>Windows Multi-Slice Detection &amp; Automated Downloader: Added multi-slice verification and an automated downloader in Inno Setup (build_windows/installer.iss) that verifies both Part 1 (-1.bin) and Part 2 (-2.bin) before extraction begins. Reason: When a user runs the installer launcher executable without the accompanying data slices in the same folder, Setup proactively detects missing slices and automatically downloads them in sequence directly from GitHub with unified progress bars.</li>
          <li>Automated GResource &amp; Dialog Regression Tests: Added regression tests in tests/test_button_recolour.py and tests/test_wikipedia_importer.py verifying GResource icon availability and initial dialog expansion behavior. Reason: Prevents future regressions and validates that custom vector icons load reliably across all target environments.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wikipedia Importer Default Expanded State: Updated on_import_wikipedia_action() in src/window.py so the dialog initializes at 920px wide with the right pane expanded (trending_revealer.set_reveal_child(True)) and immediately triggers fetch_wikipedia_top_25(). Reason: Maximizes user engagement by presenting trending topics immediately while retaining full collapse capabilities down to 450px.</li>
          <li>Inno Setup Disk Prompt Messages: Updated Inno Setup custom messages (SelectDiskTitle, SelectDiskLabel, SelectDiskLabel2, FileNotInDir2) in build_windows/installer.iss to specify the exact missing slice filename and official GitHub download link. Reason: Replaces cryptic generic "Insert Disk 2" prompts with clear, actionable download guidance.</li>
          <li>Documentation &amp; Multi-Part Windows Instructions: Updated README.md to document all three setup installer components (Launcher .exe, Part 1 .bin, and Part 2 .bin) and published formal testing documentation detailing purpose, test methodology, and pass/fail metrics (326/326 tests passing). Reason: Provides transparent quality assurance metrics and seamless installation instructions for end users.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent string to ReadAloud/1.8.19 (parolu on GitHub; contact@readaloud.app) in src/wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.19): Updated application version to 1.8.19 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_error_logger.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Native Vector Action Icon Buttons for Trending Rows: Replaced the text-based import button with a circular flat button (.trending-import-btn) housing the im.zackarious.ReadAloud.import-symbolic icon with #f6d32d hover glow. Reason: Delivers a cleaner, more intuitive Libadwaita aesthetic with instant visual recognition.</li>
          <li>Theme-Synchronized View Count Display: Placed the im.zackarious.ReadAloud.eye-symbolic vector icon inside views_box alongside the view count in .dim-label styling. Reason: Replaces raw emoji character with a clean, vector graphic that adapts seamlessly to light and dark desktop themes.</li>
          <li>Default Two-Pane Side-by-Side Wikipedia Importer: Configured the dialog to present both search and trending columns side-by-side on initial launch with the toggle button styled as "Hide Trending Topics ◀". Reason: Offers immediate visibility of trending topics while preserving a clean collapsible interface.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.18" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.18 introduces an expandable and condensable right pane on the Wikipedia Importer that scrapes the weekly Top 25 Trending topics on Wikipedia complete with rich article thumbnail preview images and one-click import, adds semi-transparent hover-activated tab navigation buttons with auto-scrolling for multi-tab document cycling, recolours primary action buttons (Open Text File, Play/Read Text, Pause, and Stop) to the signature reading highlight yellow (#f6d32d) with a crisp new scalable vector folder icon, and expands automated regression test coverage to 326 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Legacy Raster PNG Open File Icon: Removed the embedded base64 raster PNG icon for im.zackarious.ReadAloud.folder-open in data/icons and src/icons. Reason: The fixed-pixel raster image could not be styled with dynamic CSS colors and exhibited blurring at high DPI scaling; replaced with a crisp, scalable vector SVG icon matching the exact Adwaita highlight yellow (#f6d32d).</li>
          <li>Fixed Dialog Width on Wikipedia Importer: Removed fixed width constraints from the Wikipedia Importer dialog. Reason: Prevented side-by-side presentation of rich preview content; replaced with dynamic dialog resizing (450px compact, 920px wide layout) allowing seamless exploration of trending topics alongside the search interface.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wikipedia Top 25 Trending Topics Right Pane: Added an expandable sliding right pane (trending_revealer) in on_import_wikipedia_action() in src/window.py that scrapes and displays Wikipedia's official weekly Top 25 Report (Wikipedia:Top_25_Report). Reason: Gives users immediate access to popular and trending knowledge topics to read aloud without needing to brainstorm search queries.</li>
          <li>Asynchronous Article Thumbnail Image Loading: Integrated asynchronous thumbnail image fetching (fetch_thumbnail_bytes) with in-memory caching and 60x48 rounded picture displays for each trending article. Reason: Delivers rich visual context for trending topics while keeping the UI responsive and thread-safe.</li>
          <li>One-Click Trending Article Import &amp; Search Sync: Added quick "Import" action buttons on each trending row and wired row activation to populate the main search entry. Reason: Streamlines document import so users can start listening to any trending article with a single click.</li>
          <li>Live Trending Refresh &amp; Caching (fetch_wikipedia_top_25): Added 1-hour in-memory report caching and a manual refresh button (view-refresh-symbolic) in the trending pane header. Reason: Ensures instant pane re-expansion while providing on-demand live scraping of current Wikipedia reports.</li>
          <li>Hover-Activated Tab Navigation Buttons: Added semi-transparent circular navigation buttons (tab_nav_prev_btn, tab_nav_next_btn) overlaid on the tab bar that smoothly crossfade into view when 2 or more tabs are open and the user hovers over the tab bar. Reason: Enables quick, effortless cycling across multiple open tabs with automatic horizontal scroll positioning.</li>
          <li>Highlight Yellow Action Button Recolouring (#f6d32d): Recoloured the Open Text File button (open_button), Read Text button (read_button), Pause button (pause_button), and Stop button (stop_button) to match the exact yellow highlight color (#f6d32d — GNOME Adwaita Yellow 3) used during text playback. Reason: Establishes clear visual hierarchy and binds key document loading and playback action controls to the reader's active highlighting aesthetic.</li>
          <li>Scalable Vector Open Folder Icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.folder-open.svg): Designed and bundled a modern 64x64 scalable SVG icon with #f6d32d front flap and #e5a50a back tab into the GResource bundle. Reason: Guarantees high-DPI sharpness and visual consistency across all desktop scaling factors.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Test Suite Expansion (326 Tests): Added comprehensive automated tests in tests/test_button_recolour.py, tests/test_tab_navigation_buttons.py, and tests/test_wikipedia_importer.py covering Top 25 table scraping, fallback parsing, right pane expansion/collapse, row activation, quick import dispatch, button recolouring CSS, and hover navigation behavior. Reason: Guarantees long-term stability and regression resistance across all new features.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wikipedia Importer Responsive Layout: Updated on_import_wikipedia_action() in src/window.py to dynamically adapt dialog width between 450px condensed and 920px expanded layouts, smoothly adjusting parent window dimensions when needed. Reason: Provides an unconstrained, comfortable dual-pane reading and search experience across various display resolutions.</li>
          <li>Action Button State Styling (.highlight-accent-btn): Added hover (#f8e45c with 14% yellow tint), active (#e5a50a with 24% yellow tint), and disabled (38% opacity) CSS states in src/window.py. Reason: Provides smooth, accessible tactile feedback during user interaction across all primary buttons.</li>
          <li>Tab Navigation Signal Synchronization: Connected page-attached, page-detached, and page-reordered signals on the AdwTabView to automatically update navigation button sensitivity and visibility. Reason: Keeps tab navigation state strictly synchronized whenever tabs are opened, closed, or moved.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent string to ReadAloud/1.8.18 (parolu on GitHub; contact@readaloud.app) in src/wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.18): Updated application version to 1.8.18 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_error_logger.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Signature Highlight Yellow Theme Accent: Applied #f6d32d to open_button, read_button, pause_button, and stop_button, paired with the newly designed vector folder icon. Reason: Unifies the visual language of the application by echoing the editor's text reading highlight across primary control buttons.</li>
          <li>Expandable Two-Column Wikipedia Dialog: Styled the Top 25 Trending right pane with .trending-pane-card, .trending-rank-badge (#f6d32d pill), .trending-thumb (rounded image frame), and smooth slide-right revealer animation. Reason: Presents trending knowledge in a clean, organized, magazine-style overview.</li>
          <li>Hover Tab Bar Chevrons (.tab-nav-btn): Styled semi-transparent circular buttons with translucent backdrop blur (alpha(@window_bg_color, 0.76)), subtle drop shadow, and smooth hover scale feedback. Reason: Delivers non-intrusive, floating navigation controls that appear only when hovering over multiple open tabs.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.17" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.17 introduces an automatic tag removal system with a persistent toggle under Tools that sanitizes documents on import and strips bracketed notes, citations, markdown pipes, hashes, and stars in real time as the user types or pastes, integrates a permanent, fully circular font zoom control capsule with 20% zoom increments directly into the tab bar preceding the New Tab button, adds hover-activated tab navigation buttons for effortless multi-tab cycling, and expands automated regression test coverage to 316 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Ephemeral Editor Hover Font Zoom Overlay: Removed the hover revealer overlay over the main text editor (font_zoom_revealer) that required 1.5 seconds of stationary cursor hover. Reason: The overlay was prone to accidentally disappearing when moving the cursor across widget boundaries towards the zoom buttons, hindering usability.</li>
          <li>10% Font Zoom Granularity: Removed 10% incremental steps for font resizing in zoom_in() and zoom_out(). Reason: Scaled font sizes too slowly across larger reading displays; replaced with a more efficient and noticeable 20% step.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Automatic All-Tag Removal Toggle (win.auto-remove-tags): Added a stateful menu action under Tools &gt; "Automatically Remove All Tags", default-enabled, and persisted in settings.json. Reason: Enables users to automatically strip parenthetical notes ( ), bracketed citations [ ], markdown pipes | |, heading hashes #, and emphasis stars * without manually triggering individual cleaning tools.</li>
          <li>Auto-Enable on Import Workflows: Added automatic activation of win.auto-remove-tags whenever a user opens a file via File Open dialog, drags and drops documents onto the window, or triggers Wikipedia import. Reason: Guarantees imported text is immediately sanitized for speech synthesis without requiring manual pre-processing.</li>
          <li>Real-Time Typing &amp; Pasting Tag Sanitization: Added real-time keypress interception and cursor tag completion (# and * blocked; closing ), ], | strips tag and whitespace; clipboard paste sanitizes all tags). Reason: Keeps document text clean for speech synthesis as the user writes or copies text into the editor.</li>
          <li>Tab Bar Font Zoom Capsule (font_zoom_popup): Added a permanent zoom pill control ([-], percentage readout, [+]) inside AdwTabBar.end-action-widget immediately preceding the New Tab button (new_tab_button). Reason: Provides permanent, logical, and ergonomic access to document text sizing at all times without cluttering the text editor canvas.</li>
          <li>Hover-Activated Tab Navigation Buttons: Added semi-transparent circular left and right navigation buttons (tab_nav_prev_btn, tab_nav_next_btn) housed within crossfade revealers overlaid on the tab bar. They smoothly appear when multiple tabs are open and the user hovers over the tab bar, allowing quick cycling between adjacent tabs and automatically scrolling overflowing tabs into view. Reason: Dramatically simplifies horizontal navigation when working with numerous overflowing tabs.</li>
          <li>20% Font Zoom Increment: Updated zoom_in() and zoom_out() in src/window.py to increase or decrease text font size by 20% per action (buttons, Ctrl + / Ctrl -, and Ctrl + Mouse Scroll Wheel). Reason: Delivers faster, more noticeable font size changes per click while respecting 70% to 1000% bounds.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Tests (316 Tests): Added 19 unit tests in tests/test_auto_remove_tags_and_font_popup.py and 6 unit tests in tests/test_tab_navigation_buttons.py covering toggle persistence, import triggers, real-time typing/pasting tag stripping, tab bar zoom positioning, permanent visibility, circular styling, 20% zoom steps, and hover tab navigation. Reason: Prevents future regressions and validates all new accessibility features.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Document Loading Flow: Updated open_file_complete(), _on_files_dropped(), on_import_wikipedia_action(), and create_new_tab() to pass incoming text through clean_all_tags() when auto_remove_tags is active. Reason: Ensures all document loading pathways produce clean speech-ready text.</li>
          <li>Clean Symbols for Zoom Buttons: Updated decrease and increase icons to list-remove-symbolic and list-add-symbolic in src/window.ui. Reason: Replaces boxed zoom icons with clean plus and minus symbols that match modern GNOME HIG design.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent string to ReadAloud/1.8.17 (parolu on GitHub; contact@readaloud.app) in src/wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.17): Updated application version to 1.8.17 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_error_logger.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Permanent Tab Bar Zoom Capsule (.font-zoom-tab-bar): Implemented a sleek capsule styling (border-radius: 9999px; background: alpha(currentColor, 0.06); border: 1px solid alpha(currentColor, 0.12)) integrated directly into the document tab bar. Reason: Blends naturally with AdwTabBar aesthetics while keeping zoom controls immediately accessible.</li>
          <li>Semi-Transparent Hover Tab Navigation Chevrons (.tab-nav-btn): Added smooth 28x28px circular buttons styled with alpha(@window_bg_color, 0.76) and drop shadows that fade in at the left and right edges of the tab bar upon hover. Reason: Provides elegant, non-intrusive tab navigation controls without displacing the document tab strip.</li>
          <li>Fully Circular Zoom Buttons (.circular): Styled font_decrease_btn and font_increase_btn with .circular and min-width: 28px; min-height: 28px; border-radius: 9999px. Reason: Replaces rectangular button targets with perfectly circular buttons with smooth hover feedback.</li>
          <li>Bold Percentage Readout in Tab Bar: Styled font_zoom_label with font-weight: 600; min-width: 42px; text-align: center. Reason: Provides clear, high-contrast feedback of the current zoom level at a glance.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.16" date="2026-11-10">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.16 introduces a dynamic animated playback popup toolbar positioned directly above the bottom fixed toolbar—housing Pause, Rewind 15s, Forward 15s, and Stop controls that automatically slide into view during playback and collapse when idle to maximize document workspace—adds keyboard seek shortcuts (Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right), fixes redundant GStreamer bus signal watch cleanup warnings during playback termination and speed changes, and expands automated regression test coverage to 291 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Static Playback Controls on Fixed Bottom Toolbar: Removed the permanent placement of the pause button on the fixed bottom navigation bar in src/window.ui and src/window.py. Reason: Relocating playback actions to a contextual popup toolbar frees horizontal space for language, voice, and speed controls while eliminating UI clutter when the application is idle.</li>
          <li>Redundant GStreamer Bus Signal Watch Cleanup: Removed duplicate calls to bus.remove_signal_watch() across src/reader.py and src/audio_backend.py. Reason: Calling remove_signal_watch() twice on the same GStreamer message bus during playback stops or speed changes produced unnecessary "GStreamer-CRITICAL: Bus has no signal watches attached" warnings in standard error.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Dedicated Playback Popup Toolbar (playback_toolbar_revealer): Added a centered floating capsule toolbar above the fixed bottom bar in src/window.ui and src/window.py using a GtkRevealer with slide-up transition that smoothly animates into view during speech playback and collapses when idle. Reason: Provides focused, dedicated access to in-flight playback actions without taking up persistent screen estate when not in use.</li>
          <li>Rewind 15 Seconds &amp; Forward 15 Seconds Seek Controls: Added dedicated 15-second skip backward (media-seek-backward-symbolic) and forward (media-seek-forward-symbolic) buttons and shortcuts (Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right) wired to seek_playback(-15) and seek_playback(15) in src/window.py and src/window.ui. Reason: Enables users to quickly review misunderstood sentences or jump ahead in long documents during playback without losing text highlight synchronization.</li>
          <li>Bus Watch Lifecycle Tracking in GStreamer Player (_watch_added): Added boolean lifecycle state tracking for GStreamer message bus watches in src/audio_backend.py. Reason: Ensures remove_signal_watch() is only invoked when an active signal watch is attached to the pipeline bus, preventing GStreamer critical warnings.</li>
          <li>Automated Playback Popup &amp; Seek Regression Suite (291 Tests): Added 10 automated test cases in tests/test_playback_seek_buttons.py covering popup toolbar reveal/collapse animations, seek interval dispatch, keyboard accelerators, tab switching synchronization, and template widget layouts. Reason: Guarantees playback toolbar responsiveness and seek functionality remain stable across future releases.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Stop Playback Action Integration on Popup Toolbar: Updated the stop button (stop_button) to reside directly inside the popup toolbar adjacent to the forward seek button in src/window.ui and wired it to self.stop_playback() in src/window.py. Reason: Consolidates all playback lifecycle controls (Pause, Rewind, Forward, Stop) into a single cohesive control cluster.</li>
          <li>Adaptive Read Button Visibility on Bottom Fixed Bar: Updated _update_playback_toolbar_visibility() in src/window.py to hide the primary "Read Text" button during active playback and restore it when playback finishes or pauses. Reason: Maximizes horizontal spacing for voice model dropdowns and prevents accidental re-triggering while audio is playing.</li>
          <li>Safe Pipeline Reset in Reader (stop_audio): Updated Reader.stop_audio() in src/reader.py to immediately reset self._current_pipeline = None after stopping the active player backend. Reason: Prevents redundant secondary pipeline teardown operations from executing against already-closed audio pipelines.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.16 (parolu on GitHub; contact@readaloud.app) in src/wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.16): Updated application version to 1.8.16 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_error_logger.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Floating Playback Control Capsule Above Bottom Bar: Designed a centered capsule toolbar with .playback-popup-toolbar CSS styling, featuring rounded borders (12px), subtle theme-aware translucent fill (alpha(currentColor, 0.06)), and fine perimeter border (alpha(currentColor, 0.12)). Reason: Delivers a modern, clean visual presentation that clearly delineates temporary playback controls from persistent configuration settings.</li>
          <li>Slide-Up Revealer Animation: Configured transition-type="slide-up" on the playback revealer directly above bottom_fixed_bar. Reason: Provides fluid visual motion as the playback controls emerge smoothly upward from the fixed toolbar when playback starts and neatly collapse downward when playback finishes.</li>
          <li>Consistent 48x42 Touch Targets &amp; 25px Optical Icon Sizing: Applied 48x42px minimum size requests and 25px optical icon sizing across all popup toolbar buttons (pause_button, rewind_button, forward_button, stop_button). Reason: Ensures visual symmetry and accessible, touch-friendly click targets across all playback control buttons.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.15" date="2026-11-07">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.15 prevents silent application crashes when synthesizing large text (such as 35,000 words or long run-on sentences) by subdividing oversized text blocks to stay safely within native C++ buffer boundaries, adds persistent session tracking and startup crash detection that presents an interactive diagnostic report dialog encouraging users to report issues on GitHub, introduces a dedicated Error Log button in the About section with a full-featured log viewer and clipboard copy utility, enables Python's native faulthandler to capture low-level faults to disk, and expands the automated test suite to 281 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unbounded Sentence Synthesis in Reader: Removed direct synthesis of unbounded text blocks and sentences exceeding 250 characters or 40 words in src/reader.py. Reason: Long blocks and run-on sentences without punctuation overflowed native C++ clause buffers in piper_phonemize and espeak-ng, causing immediate silent SIGSEGV or SIGABRT crashes without error output.</li>
          <li>Uncaptured Native Crashes and Silent Exits: Removed unmonitored process termination without low-level crash diagnostics in src/error_logger.py. Reason: Native C-level segmentation faults bypassed Python's standard sys.excepthook, leaving no error log or traceback for users or developers to inspect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Safe Oversized Sentence Chunking (_split_oversized_sentence): Added automatic sentence bounding in src/reader.py that subdivides oversized sentences (&lt;= 250 characters and &lt;= 40 words) at natural punctuation marks (semicolons, colons, commas, dashes, and parentheses) while preserving exact character coordinate slices and phonetic word weights. Reason: Guarantees that Piper TTS and espeak-ng never encounter buffer overflows on large text imports (such as 35,000-word documents) while maintaining sample-accurate word highlighting during speech playback.</li>
          <li>Startup Crash Detection &amp; Diagnostic Report (check_previous_session_crash, CrashReportDialog): Added persistent session marker tracking (session_marker.json) and startup detection in src/error_logger.py and src/main.py. If ReadAloud detects an unclean exit on launch, it logs an abnormal termination report to error.log and presents an interactive CrashReportDialog. Reason: Alerts users when the application unexpectedly closed, displays what was in-flight (voice, word count, sentence progress, error log excerpt), and provides a single-click "Copy Crash Report to Clipboard" and "Report on GitHub" button to help authors debug and improve the software.</li>
          <li>Native C-Level Fault Interception (faulthandler &amp; SIGTERM): Enabled Python's faulthandler in src/error_logger.py to write low-level C stack traces directly to error.log upon receiving SIGSEGV, SIGFPE, SIGABRT, SIGBUS, or SIGILL, along with SIGTERM signal interception. Reason: Captures native crashes and external process kills into the persistent error log even when standard Python exception handlers cannot run.</li>
          <li>About Section Error Log Viewer (ErrorLogViewerDialog): Added an "Error Log" button in the About dialog's links row and implemented ErrorLogViewerDialog featuring a monospace log view, "Copy Log", "Open Folder", "Report Issue", and "Clear" actions. Reason: Provides users with direct, easy access to inspect, copy, or purge diagnostic logs at any time without having to navigate filesystem paths manually.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Test Expansion (281 Tests): Added 9 comprehensive automated tests in tests/test_error_logger.py and tests/test_about_window.py covering session marker lifecycles, crash detection, clean exit handling, error log viewing/clearing, oversized sentence splitting, 35,000-word synthesis chunking, and dialog presentation. Reason: Prevents regressions in large document synthesis, crash reporting, and log viewer stability.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Synthesis Activity Heartbeat in Reader (_synthesize_audio): Updated Reader._synthesize_audio() to record in-flight synthesis state (voice model, word count, sentence index, text snippet) to session_marker.json and cleanly reset state upon completion, cancellation, or error. Reason: Ensures crash reports accurately pinpoint the exact sentence and voice model that was being processed if an abrupt termination occurs.</li>
          <li>Clean Shutdown Hooks across Application Lifecycle: Updated ReadAloudWindow._do_close(), ReadAloudApplication._on_quit_action(), do_shutdown(), and main() to invoke mark_clean_exit(). Reason: Guarantees that intentional window closures and application exits are marked clean so normal shutdowns do not trigger false-positive crash dialogs on subsequent launches.</li>
          <li>Centralized Synthesis Error Logging: Updated Reader._synthesize_audio() exception handling to call log_error() directly to record detailed synthesis failures into error.log. Reason: Guarantees synthesis exceptions are persisted to disk even before UI error alerts are presented.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.15 (parolu on GitHub; contact@readaloud.app) in src/wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.15): Updated application version to 1.8.15 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_error_logger.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unexpected Shutdown Detected Dialog Banner: Added a warning dialog (CrashReportDialog) with a prominent warning emblem (dialog-warning-symbolic), clean title hierarchy, structured diagnostic report card, suggested-action "Copy Crash Report" button, and direct GitHub link. Reason: Provides clear visual cues and effortless one-click reporting when an unexpected application crash occurs.</li>
          <li>About Dialog Error Log Button: Integrated a pill-shaped "Error Log" button into the About tab's primary link row next to Website and Report an Issue. Reason: Offers a prominent, discoverable visual entry point for users to inspect diagnostic logs directly from the About dialog.</li>
          <li>Interactive Copy Confirmation Feedback: Added temporary "✓ Copied to Clipboard!" and "✓ Copied!" label state transitions with automatic reset on the copy buttons in CrashReportDialog and ErrorLogViewerDialog. Reason: Delivers clear, immediate visual confirmation that diagnostic details have been copied to the clipboard.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.14" date="2026-11-06">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.14 enhances the text cleanup tools workflow by eliminating the redundant "Apply to all tabs or just current tab?" modal dialog when only a single tab is open, applying text transformations directly to the active document with instant feedback, preserving multi-tab batch cleanup when multiple tabs are open, and adding automated regression test coverage.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Redundant Scope Choice Dialog on Single Open Tab: Removed the unconditional invocation of the Adw.AlertDialog modal asking "Do you wish to apply this tool to all tabs or just the current tab?" when triggering text cleanup operations with only one open document tab. Reason: Prompting the user to choose between "Current Tab" and "All Tabs" when there is only 1 tab in the workspace is unnecessary, redundant, and interrupts user workflow since no other document tabs exist.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Direct Single-Tab Tool Execution (_prompt_and_apply_bracket_tool): Added a tab count check (self.tab_view.get_n_pages() &lt;= 1) in src/window.py to immediately execute cleanup tools (Remove ( ) Brackets, Remove [ ] Brackets, Remove | Pipes, Remove # Hashes, Remove * Stars, and Remove All) directly on the active tab's text buffer (_apply_bracket_tool_to_current_tab()) without showing a dialog. Reason: Streamlines single-document text cleaning workflows with instant, zero-click execution while seamlessly preserving the multi-tab prompt whenever more than one tab is open.</li>
          <li>Automated Single-Tab Dialog Bypass Regression Tests: Added dedicated unit tests (test_prompt_and_apply_bracket_tool_single_tab_bypasses_dialog and test_prompt_and_apply_bracket_tool_multi_tab_prompts_dialog) in tests/test_text_tools.py verifying that single-tab tool invocations never spawn an Adw.AlertDialog modal and that multi-tab sessions retain the scope selection dialog. Reason: Prevents regressions in modal popup handling across text manipulation actions in single-tab and multi-tab workflows.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.14 format with repository origin and contact metadata in wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.14): Updated application version to 1.8.14 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Suppression of Redundant Modal Popup on Single Tab: Eliminated the centered Adw.AlertDialog popup dialog when running text cleanup actions on single-tab workspaces, keeping the editor buffer fully focused without modal dimming or extra clicks. Reason: Provides a cleaner, smoother, and uninterrupted user interface that adheres to desktop Human Interface Guidelines for context-appropriate dialogs.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.13" date="2026-11-04">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.13 resolves a critical audio playback resumption issue where switching tabs or opening a new tab with the plus button paused audio but returning to the tab restarted playback from the beginning of the buffer; adds per-tab playback and paused state tracking, anchors pause marks and cursor positions at the paused word in the text buffer, preserves visual word highlighting across tab switches, synchronizes dynamic playback controls per tab, supports seamless resumption from both Resume and Read buttons as well as keyboard shortcuts, and expands the automated regression test suite to 270 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Abrupt Tab Playback Reset on Tab Switch: Removed the unconditional stop_playback() invocation in _on_selected_page_changed() when switching active tabs. Reason: Abruptly stopping playback cleared the audio player pipeline, destroyed the pause anchor mark, and reset reading position to offset 0, preventing users from resuming audio where they left off when returning to the tab.</li>
          <li>Default Cursor Fallback to Offset 0 in read_text(): Removed the unconditioned fallback that placed the cursor iterator at character offset 0 when no text was selected and pause_resume_mark was present. Reason: Ignored existing anchored paused positions, forcing playback synthesis to restart from the beginning of the buffer even when a tab had been cleanly paused.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Per-Tab Playback State Management (_active_tab_page, _is_playing, _is_paused, _paused_offset, _highlight_index): Added per-page playback metadata and active tab reference tracking in window.py. Reason: Enables each document tab to maintain its own independent audio playback, paused state, exact character offset, and active word highlight index across tab switches and new tab creations.</li>
          <li>Non-Destructive Tab Audio Pausing on Switch (_on_selected_page_changed): Added automatic pausing (reader.pause_audio()) and state persistence when switching away from an active tab (such as clicking the + button to create a new tab or selecting a different tab). Reason: Pauses the audio stream without destroying the underlying pipeline or clearing the visual word highlight, allowing instant and sample-accurate resumption upon returning.</li>
          <li>Text-Anchored Pause Mark &amp; Cursor Placement on Inactive Tab: Added automated creation and positioning of pause_resume_mark (Gtk.TextMark) along with place_cursor() at the exact paused character offset in the outgoing tab's text buffer. Reason: Anchors the paused reading location to the text buffer even across tab switches and ensures the cursor stays synchronized with the paused word.</li>
          <li>Automated Tab Playback Regression Tests (test_tab_switch_pauses_playback, test_new_tab_pauses_playback_and_resume_on_return, test_new_tab_pauses_playback_and_resume_with_new_voice_settings): Added regression tests in tests/test_tab_system.py and tests/test_cached_playback.py covering tab creation during playback, paused state and highlight retention, and resumption on return. Reason: Prevents regressions where switching tabs or creating new documents could reset playback or discard paused positions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Play &amp; Resume Interaction in read_text(): Updated read_text() to detect if the current tab is in a paused state (self.is_playing and self.is_paused) and seamlessly call toggle_pause() to resume audio, and updated cursor iteration to honor pause_resume_mark if present. Reason: Guarantees that clicking the Play button ("Read Text"), clicking Resume, or pressing Ctrl+P resumes playback directly from where the user left off without restarting from the beginning.</li>
          <li>Highlight Timer Synchronization on Tab Resume (toggle_pause): Updated toggle_pause() to restart the word highlight polling timer (_highlight_timeout_id) if inactive and sync cur_page._is_paused = False when resuming audio. Reason: Ensures visual word highlighting resumes scrolling and tracking the spoken audio seamlessly when playback is resumed after returning to a paused tab.</li>
          <li>Tab Close Resource Deallocation (_on_close_page): Updated finish_close() to invoke reader.stop_audio() and clear _active_tab_page when closing a tab with an active or paused reader. Reason: Prevents orphaned background GStreamer pipelines or temporary audio files from lingering after a tab is closed.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.13 format with repository origin and contact metadata in wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.13): Updated application version to 1.8.13 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_windows/build_arm64_portable.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/build_appimage.sh, build_linux/debian/control, build_macos/build_macos.sh, tests/test_about_window.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Word Highlight Retention on Outgoing Tab: Preserved the active word highlight (current_word_highlight tag and HighlightTextView._highlight_range) on the tab being switched away from, instead of clearing it. Reason: Gives the user immediate visual confirmation of where they left off reading when returning to the document tab.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Playback Control Synchronization per Tab: Updated _on_selected_page_changed() to synchronize toolbar button icons and tooltips dynamically when switching between tabs (showing Resume icon and enabling the pause button when selecting a paused tab, and showing idle Play button with disabled pause button when selecting an unplayed tab). Reason: Provides clear visual affordances so users immediately recognize whether the active tab has paused playback ready to resume or is ready for fresh reading.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.12" date="2026-11-02">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.12 streamlines the window header bar controls by removing the redundant burger-like unwrap button following the Save to Text File icon, preserves document unwrapping via standard shortcuts and the primary application menu, introduces automated header bar layout test verification, recompiles application resources, and updates the version across all platforms and package builders.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Redundant Left-Side Header Bar Burger / Unwrap Button: Removed the unwrap_button (format-justify-fill-symbolic) widget located immediately after the Save to Text File icon in window.ui along with its @Gtk.Template.Child binding in window.py. Reason: The four-line justification symbol visually resembled a duplicate burger menu on the left side of the header bar directly adjacent to document action buttons, causing visual clutter and user confusion with the main application burger menu on the right. Text unwrapping and paragraph reflow remain fully accessible through the primary menu ("Unwrap / Reflow Text") and via keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+Shift+W, Ctrl+J).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Header Bar Button Configuration Test (test_headerbar_buttons): Added a dedicated regression test in tests/test_word_wrap.py verifying that the header bar's start child container strictly contains Open File (open_button), Wikipedia Import (wiki_button), and Save Text (save_text_button), and asserting that the redundant unwrap button is not present on the header bar. Reason: Guarantees that future updates maintain a clean, uncluttered header bar layout and prevents accidental reintroduction of redundant toolbar buttons.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.12 format with repository origin and contact metadata in wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version release.</li>
          <li>Compiled GResource Bundle: Recompiled src/readaloud.gresource with glib-compile-resources from src/readaloud.gresource.xml. Reason: Packages the updated window.ui header bar definition into the application's runtime binary resource bundle.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.12): Updated application version to 1.8.12 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/debian/control, tests/test_about_window.py, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Uncluttered Header Bar Navigation: Streamlined the top header bar layout by eliminating the duplicate burger-style icon between the Save to Text File icon and the centered window title. Reason: Restores a balanced, clean user interface with standard GNOME HIG alignment, eliminating visual distraction while keeping core reading, saving, and navigation tools cleanly distinct.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.11" date="2026-11-01">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.11 resolves critical audio playback silence and missing element errors on Windows by introducing dynamic GStreamer audio sink discovery, adds a zero-dependency native Windows fallback player (WinSoundAudioPlayer) and Unix CLI fallback player (SubprocessAudioPlayer), establishes a resilient multi-tier audio player fallback chain in Reader, fixes the unhandled AttributeError crash when pressing Return in the Wikipedia importer dialog, updates PyInstaller packaging to harvest PortAudio binaries and sounddevice data, includes GStreamer audio sink plugins in Windows CI builds, and expands the automated regression test suite to 267 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Hardcoded GStreamer "autoaudiosink" Pipeline Construction: Removed hardcoded autoaudiosink element in reader.py and audio_backend.py. Reason: Systems lacking gst-plugins-good (such as Windows environments without good plugins installed) fail with gst_parse_error: no element "autoaudiosink", causing playback pipeline creation to fail completely with silence.</li>
          <li>Bypassed Audio Backend Architecture in Reader: Removed direct, unabstracted GStreamer calls in Reader._play_audio_file_async() that bypassed audio_backend.py. Reason: Bypassing the audio backend prevented Reader from using alternative audio players (sounddevice, winsound, CLI tools) when GStreamer was absent or broken.</li>
          <li>Nonexistent AlertDialog.response() Invocation: Removed dialog.response("import") in window.py on the Wikipedia import entry activate handler. Reason: Adw.AlertDialog is a Gtk.Widget in Libadwaita and does not possess a .response() method (unlike legacy Gtk.Dialog or Adw.MessageDialog), which caused pressing Return or Keypad Enter in the search input to throw AttributeError: 'AlertDialog' object has no attribute 'response' and crash the main thread.</li>
          <li>Unguarded Multi-Module Pre-Initialization in Windows Entrypoint: Removed the monolithic try...except block importing all C-extensions in a single block in win_entrypoint.py. Reason: If any single module (e.g. sounddevice due to missing _sounddevice_data) failed to import, the entire block aborted, preventing subsequent extensions (lameenc) from pre-initializing before MinGW64 GLib runtime DLLs loaded.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Dynamic GStreamer Audio Sink Detection (get_best_gst_audio_sink &amp; get_gst_audio_sink_candidates): Added dynamic GStreamer audio sink discovery in audio_backend.py querying registered element factories in order of platform preference (autoaudiosink, wasapisink, directsoundsink, pulsesink, pipewiresink, alsasink, osxaudiosink). Reason: Automatically detects and utilizes whichever audio sink plugin is installed on the user's host platform instead of assuming autoaudiosink is always present.</li>
          <li>Sequential GStreamer Sink Fallback Recovery: Added multi-sink trial iteration in GStreamerAudioPlayer.play(). Reason: If the primary sink fails during pipeline launch or state transition, the player attempts remaining available sinks sequentially before failing.</li>
          <li>Native Windows Standard-Library Audio Player (WinSoundAudioPlayer): Added WinSoundAudioPlayer in audio_backend.py implementing BaseAudioPlayer using Python's built-in winsound module. Reason: Provides a zero-dependency, guaranteed audio output mechanism on Microsoft Windows that requires no external GStreamer plugins or PortAudio binaries, ensuring speech is always audible.</li>
          <li>CLI Subprocess Audio Player (SubprocessAudioPlayer): Added SubprocessAudioPlayer in audio_backend.py using system tools (aplay, paplay, pw-play, ffplay). Reason: Delivers an additional playback fallback on Linux/Unix systems where GStreamer or sounddevice may not be available.</li>
          <li>Multi-Tier Audio Player Fallback Chain (get_audio_player_chain): Added an ordered fallback player chain in audio_backend.py and integrated it into Reader._play_audio_file_async(). Reason: Seamlessly falls back to secondary and tertiary audio players if the primary player fails to launch, eliminating silent synthesis failures.</li>
          <li>PortAudio and GStreamer Dependencies in Windows CI: Added mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-portaudio, mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gstreamer, mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gst-plugins-base, mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gst-plugins-good, and mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gst-plugins-bad to build-windows.yml. Reason: Ensures Windows release builds include essential audio sink plugins (autoaudiosink, directsoundsink, wasapisink) and PortAudio libraries.</li>
          <li>PyInstaller Hook Collection for PortAudio &amp; Sounddevice: Added collect_all('sounddevice') and collect_all('_sounddevice_data'), portaudio DLL search, and plugin binary collections in ReadAloud.spec. Reason: Resolves ModuleNotFoundError: No module named '_sounddevice_data' in frozen Windows bundles.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Test Suite Expansion (267 Tests): Added tests/test_audio_playback_fallback.py and entry activation unit tests, increasing test coverage from 258 to 267 automated unit tests. Reason: Guarantees verification of sink discovery, fallback chains, and dialog activation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reader Audio Architecture Synchronization: Updated Reader methods (pause_audio, resume_audio, get_playback_position, seek, stop_audio) to delegate directly to self._player while keeping _current_pipeline synchronized for legacy and test callers. Reason: Guarantees that word highlight synchronization, seek navigation, and pause/resume work uniformly regardless of which audio backend is active.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Importer Return Key Activation: Updated the article search entry's activate signal handler in window.py to validate input, emit dialog.emit("response", "import"), and invoke dialog.force_close(). Reason: Allows users to press Return or Keypad Enter in the search box to import the article immediately without triggering AttributeError.</li>
          <li>Isolated Windows Pre-Init Extension Loading: Updated win_entrypoint.py to import C-extensions in an iterative loop with per-module exception trapping and configured _sounddevice_data PortAudio DLL directory search. Reason: Prevents transient import issues in one extension from cascading and blocking other required libraries.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification string to ReadAloud/1.8.11 format with repository origin and contact metadata in wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Maintains strict compliance with Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent policies for the new version.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.11): Updated application version to 1.8.11 across meson.build, src/main.py, src/error_logger.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, build_linux/build_deb.sh, build_linux/debian/control, and CI workflows. Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Responsive Wikipedia Search Entry Form Submission: Fixed the Wikipedia article import modal visual responsiveness upon pressing Return or Keypad Enter in the topic entry box, ensuring the dialog immediately dismisses and seamlessly transitions to the loading progress spinner without unhandled exception popups or freezing. Reason: Delivers a smooth, frictionless keyboard interaction for article lookups matching native Libadwaita dialog behaviors.</li>
          <li>Persistent Real-Time Word Highlighting Across Audio Backends: Maintained visual yellow word-level text highlighting during speech playback across all fallback audio engines (SoundDeviceAudioPlayer, WinSoundAudioPlayer, SubprocessAudioPlayer, GStreamerAudioPlayer). Reason: Ensures visual reading assistance remains active and responsive even when running on minimal fallback audio backends.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.10" date="2026-10-30">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.10 introduces automatic paragraph gap separation with an empty line gap between paragraphs upon pressing Return or Keypad Enter, integrates paragraph gap normalization for all document imports and clipboard pastes, incorporates a direct Wikipedia article importer into the Tools menu and header bar, adds an interactive live autocomplete suggestions dropdown matching Wikipedia's website design with article thumbnails and descriptions, enables multi-tab sequential import for related Wikipedia topics with automatic all-tag stripping, embeds the Wikipedia globe logo and a Wikimedia Foundation donation callout card, fixes the broken Open File dialog by eliminating gettext function shadowing, establishes a Wikimedia policy-compliant HTTP client with a resilient standard-library fallback, resolves Flatpak packaging build and site-packages cleanup issues, eliminates premature cancellation when closing modal progress dialogs, modernizes error reporting with native Adw.AlertDialog modals, and expands the automated regression test suite to 244 tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Single-Newline Paragraph Collapse on Return Key: Removed default Gtk.TextView single-newline Return key insertion behavior that placed new lines directly adjacent without vertical spacing. Reason: Tightly packed lines without an empty line gap between paragraphs make it harder for users to distinguish distinct paragraphs visually while text is being spoken and highlighted during speech playback.</li>
          <li>Unformatted Single-Newline Text Imports and Pastes: Removed unspaced single-newline document loading and raw clipboard pasting that inserted dense, unformatted paragraphs into the reader. Reason: Raw single-newline text resulted in cramped, hard-to-follow text during speech synthesis; enforcing consistent double-newline gaps between paragraphs makes text substantially easier to follow during audio playback.</li>
          <li>Gettext Function Parameter Shadowing in File Dialogs: Removed parameter names "_" in open_file_dialog and save_text_dialog that shadowed Python's _() translation function with None. Reason: When Gio simple actions triggered open_file_dialog(self, action, _), Gio passed None for the parameter, binding "_" to None. Subsequent calls to _("Supported Documents...") crashed with TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not callable, rendering the Open File button completely inoperative.</li>
          <li>Direct Browser User-Agent Impersonation in Wikipedia Requests: Removed the spoofed Mozilla/5.0 browser user-agent header from wikipedia_importer.py. Reason: Impersonating a standard browser without client contact metadata violated Wikimedia Foundation's User-Agent Policy, causing Wikipedia's edge firewalls to flag requests as automated bot abuse and block downloads with HTTP 403 Forbidden.</li>
          <li>Premature Operation Cancellation on Programmatic Dialog Close: Removed the unrestricted response handler assignment in _start_wikipedia_import that marked operations as cancelled whenever progress_dialog.force_close() was called. Reason: In Libadwaita, force_close() triggers the dialog's close response ("cancel"), which previously caused the completion callback to interpret programmatic closure as a user cancel action, immediately returning and discarding scraped articles before tabs could be populated.</li>
          <li>Wildcard Python Library Cleanup Directives in Flatpak Manifest: Removed the "cleanup": ["*"] directives from python3-meson-python and python3-scikit-build in pip-dependencies.json. Reason: The wildcard cleanup directive deleted the entire /app/lib/python3.13/site-packages directory after building build backends, purging installed runtime dependencies and causing ReadAloud to crash on launch with ModuleNotFoundError.</li>
          <li>PEP 517 Source Distribution Build Dependency in Flatpak: Removed .tar.gz source tarball archives for beautifulsoup4 and soupsieve in pip-dependencies.json. Reason: Building from source tarballs required the hatchling PEP 517 build backend, which is absent from the standard GNOME Flatpak runtime and caused pip build failures.</li>
          <li>Deprecated Gtk.MessageDialog Error Modals: Removed deprecated Gtk.MessageDialog instances and legacy .show() method calls in _show_error(). Reason: Gtk.MessageDialog is deprecated in GTK 4.10+ and failed to render properly as a modal sheet within Libadwaita application windows.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Return Key Stroke Paragraph Gap Separation (HighlightTextView._on_key_pressed): Added a dedicated keyboard controller to HighlightTextView intercepting Return and Keypad Enter to insert \n\n (a separate line with an empty line gap), deleting active selections and wrapping mutations in begin_user_action() / end_user_action() for clean single-step undo/redo, while retaining Shift + Return for single newlines. Reason: Automatically creates visually clear paragraph gaps as the user types without requiring manual double-tapping of the Return key.</li>
          <li>Automatic Paragraph Gap Normalization Utility (ensure_paragraph_gaps): Added a text processing engine in src/window.py that converts single newlines into double newlines (\n\n), cleans whitespace on blank lines, normalizes CRLF/CR line endings, and limits excessive newlines to 2. Reason: Guarantees consistent and readable paragraph separation across all imported, pasted, and edited text.</li>
          <li>Clipboard Paste Paragraph Formatting (HighlightTextView._on_paste_clipboard): Added clipboard paste interception for GTK's paste-clipboard signal (Ctrl + V, Shift + Insert, and context menu Paste) that asynchronously retrieves clipboard contents and formats text via ensure_paragraph_gaps(). Reason: Ensures all text copied and pasted from external applications immediately adopts readable paragraph gap spacing.</li>
          <li>Imported Document Paragraph Formatting: Integrated ensure_paragraph_gaps() across tab creation (create_new_tab), File Open (open_file_complete), Drag &amp; Drop file loaders, EPUB/PDF chapter extractors, Wikipedia imports, and demo presets. Reason: Enforces consistent paragraph spacing for all imported documents regardless of format or source.</li>
          <li>Live Wikipedia Search Autocomplete Dropdown (fetch_wikipedia_suggestions): Added real-time autocomplete suggestions to the search box in the Wikipedia import window backed by Wikipedia's official REST Search API, returning matching articles with thumbnail previews, bold titles, and subtitle descriptions. Reason: Enables users to quickly search, discover, and pick exact Wikipedia article titles without leaving the application or memorizing precise spelling.</li>
          <li>In-Memory Thumbnail Caching (fetch_thumbnail_bytes): Added thread-safe in-memory caching for Wikipedia article thumbnails. Reason: Avoids duplicate network requests and eliminates latency when browsing or re-querying common search suggestions.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Quick-Access Header Bar Button (wiki_button): Added a dedicated Wikipedia import button in the top-left corner of the main window headerbar directly after the Open File button, styled with the Wikipedia globe puzzle logo and standardized (48, 42) dimensions. Reason: Provides one-click access to the Wikipedia article importer without needing to navigate into the burger menu.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia Foundation Donation Callout Card: Added a non-intrusive donation callout card inside the Wikipedia import dialog featuring a direct hyperlink button to the Wikimedia Foundation donation portal. Reason: Encourages users to support the Wikimedia Foundation and keep free knowledge accessible to everyone worldwide.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Article Importer (wikipedia_importer.py): Added a complete Wikipedia scraping and article extraction module capable of normalizing article topic names (e.g. "Artificial Intelligence", "Donald Trump") and full Wikipedia URLs into clean, structured markdown. Reason: Allows users to import Wikipedia articles directly into ReadAloud for offline listening without manually copying and pasting text from web browsers.</li>
          <li>Tools Menu Wikipedia Action (win.import-wikipedia): Added "Import Wikipedia Article…" to the Tools submenu in src/window.ui, wired to on_import_wikipedia_action() in src/window.py. Reason: Provides easy and discoverable access to article imports directly alongside existing document and text cleanup tools.</li>
          <li>Multi-Tab Related Topic Extraction: Added automatic discovery of internal related /wiki/... article links with a configurable spin button (1–10 articles) in the import dialog, creating a distinct tab for each related article. Reason: Enables research workflows where a main subject and its related references are imported into sequential tabs in one single operation.</li>
          <li>Dual-Engine Resilient HTTP Client: Added standard-library urllib.request fallback logic to fetch_wikipedia_article() if requests is unavailable or encounters connection exceptions. Reason: Ensures reliable HTTP fetching across containerized runtimes and environments without third-party network libraries.</li>
          <li>Standard-Library HTMLParser Fallback: Added _WikipediaHTMLParser to wikipedia_importer.py to parse and clean Wikipedia article structures without requiring BeautifulSoup. Reason: Guarantees that Wikipedia article parsing continues to operate smoothly even if bs4 is missing from the environment.</li>
          <li>Pre-built Pure-Python Universal Wheels for Flatpak: Added pre-built universal .whl packages for beautifulsoup4 and soupsieve to pip-dependencies.json. Reason: Eliminates build-time compiler dependencies and ensures fast, clean Flatpak installations.</li>
          <li>Automated Test Suite Expansion (244 Tests): Added 15 comprehensive automated unit tests covering paragraph gap normalization, Return key presses, Keypad Enter, Shift + Return, selection replacement, non-editable text views, clipboard paste formatting, and tab imports, expanding the test suite to 244 automated unit tests. Reason: Guarantees full regression prevention for paragraph gap rules, keyboard shortcuts, and document imports.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Document Buffer Population and Tab Creation: Updated create_new_tab(), _import_dropped_files_into_empty_tab(), _on_import_choice_response(), _apply_and_play_demo(), _on_wikipedia_import_selected(), and open_file_complete() to format text with ensure_paragraph_gaps(). Reason: Standardizes paragraph spacing across every document loading, file dropping, demo loading, and scraping flow in the application.</li>
          <li>Undo/Redo Grouping on Paragraph Insertion: Updated Return key insertion and clipboard paste handlers to wrap buffer mutations in begin_user_action() and end_user_action(). Reason: Allows users to undo or redo typed paragraph gaps and formatted pastes in a single Ctrl + Z / Ctrl + Y keystroke instead of multi-step undo operations.</li>
          <li>Open File Dialog and Save Dialog Callback Signatures: Updated open_file_dialog and save_text_dialog method signatures to (self, action=None, param=None). Reason: Resolves the critical Open File button crash, allowing file selection and text saving dialogs to open without exception.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Search Box Debouncing and Navigation: Updated the search box with a 250ms debouncer, Down Arrow focus shifting into the suggestions listbox, Enter key selection, Escape key dismissal, and automatic dropdown suppression on full URLs. Reason: Provides a smooth, responsive, and accessible keyboard-first search experience without spamming network endpoints during keystrokes.</li>
          <li>Dropdown Scroll and View Adjustment: Updated the suggestions container to use a responsive Gtk.ScrolledWindow with min-content-height: 140px and automatic scroll reset to the top. Reason: Keeps 2–3 suggestions in view while preventing the modal from expanding excessively or pushing dialog controls off-screen.</li>
          <li>Automatic All-Tag Stripping on Wikipedia Import: Updated the tab population pipeline (_populate_wikipedia_tabs) so that every fetched article automatically undergoes clean_all_tags() before buffer insertion, removing brackets, pipes, wikitables, hashes, and asterisks. Reason: Formats raw Wikipedia text into smooth, natural, and pronunciation-ready prose for Piper TTS synthesis.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia-Compliant User-Agent Header: Updated user-agent identification to conforming project contact headers strictly meeting the Wikimedia Foundation User-Agent Policy. Reason: Ensures uninterrupted network access and compliant programmatic communication with Wikipedia API and web endpoints.</li>
          <li>Worker Exception Scoping in Asynchronous Importer: Updated error capturing in _start_wikipedia_import to bind err_msg = str(err) prior to dispatching GLib.idle_add(). Reason: Prevents Python 3 free variable NameError exceptions resulting from automatic variable cleanup at the end of except blocks.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.10): Updated application version to 1.8.10 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, src/wikipedia_importer.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reader Paragraph Spacing and Vertical Layout: Updated the document text reader view so that all paragraphs are visually separated by an empty line gap (\n\n) when typing with Return, pasting, or importing documents. Reason: Provides generous, clear vertical separation between paragraphs, making it substantially easier for users to read along as words and sentences are highlighted during audio playback.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Search Dropdown Card: Added an expandable suggestions listbox underneath the search box styled with .card and .rich-list, showing article thumbnails, bold headings, and dimmed description captions matching the Wikipedia website layout. Reason: Visualizes search matches and allows immediate visual identification of articles before importing.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Globe Quick-Access Button in Header Bar: Added a dedicated Wikipedia icon button to the top-left header bar between the Open and Save buttons, featuring the clean Wikipedia globe puzzle logo, header-icon-btn CSS styling, and (48, 42) sizing. Reason: Makes Wikipedia imports immediately accessible from the main interface while keeping header controls visually balanced.</li>
          <li>Wikipedia Globe Logo in Dialogs: Embedded the high-resolution, alpha-transparent Wikipedia globe logo (/im/zackarious/ReadAloud/images/wikipedia-logo.png) centered in the import dialog and in the asynchronous fetching progress dialog. Reason: Provides clear, professional branding identifying the source of imported content.</li>
          <li>Wikimedia Donation Encouragement Card: Added a styled .card container in the import dialog displaying an encouragement message and a centered button linking to the Wikimedia Foundation donation portal. Reason: Promotes awareness of the non-profit foundation maintaining Wikipedia with an aesthetically integrated donation prompt.</li>
          <li>Asynchronous Download Spinner Dialog: Added an active Gtk.Spinner modal alert displaying real-time fetching progress (e.g. "Fetching 'Donald_Trump'…") with a responsive Cancel button. Reason: Provides clear visual feedback during network operations without freezing the main user interface.</li>
          <li>Native Adw.AlertDialog Error Presentation: Updated _show_error() to present native Adw.AlertDialog modals with Libadwaita styling and a standard OK response button. Reason: Replaces outdated unstyled message dialogs with polished, theme-integrated alert sheets.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.9" date="2026-10-16">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.9 redesigns the "About ReadAloud" window into a condensed sub-tabbed dialog matching the GNOME Disks GTK4 style with a centered segmented pill switcher, introduces star (asterisk) tag stripping for markdown bold, italics, bullets, and horizontal dividers, adds a unified "Remove All" option directly under the Tools submenu, expands drag-and-drop import tag stripping to 5 options, and increases automated regression test coverage to 210 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Monolithic About Dialog and Multi-Level Drill-Down Subpages: Removed the oversized Adw.AboutWindow implementation and its nested navigation views (whatsnew, details, legal) that required clicking back-and-forth into separate subpages to read changelogs, application description, and legal terms. Reason: The monolithic dialog was excessively tall (600x750px), cramped vertical scrolling within deep navigation pages, and hid important project information behind nested navigation rows.</li>
          <li>Sequential Single-Tool Tag Cleanup Constraint: Removed the restriction requiring users to select each bracket, pipe, and hash removal tool one-by-one sequentially from the menu. Reason: Cleaning complex markdown documents containing combinations of brackets, tables, hashes, and asterisks forced users to open the burger menu up to 4 separate times.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Condensed Sub-Tabbed "About ReadAloud" Window (AboutReadAloudWindow): Added a dedicated AboutReadAloudWindow featuring a centered segmented pill switcher (Gtk.StackSwitcher with .linked style) in the headerbar with 5 immediate sub-tabs: About, Change Logs, Description, Credits, and Legal, preserving 100% of all project information with zero data loss. Reason: Provides a compact (~600x680px), modern, and easily navigable interface that conforms to GNOME HIG dialog standards without burying information.</li>
          <li>Star (Asterisk) Tag Stripping Tool (clean_star_symbols): Added clean_star_symbols() in src/window.py and registered win.remove-stars ("Remove * Stars (Asterisks)") in the Tools menu. Reason: Strips markdown bold, italic, bullet, footnote, and horizontal divider asterisks (*, **, ***) while normalizing whitespace and punctuation spacing, preventing speech synthesizers from pronouncing punctuation symbols or stumbling over formatting characters.</li>
          <li>Star (Asterisk) Import Dialog Checkbox: Added "Remove * stars (asterisks)" as a 5th checkbox option in _create_tag_stripping_checkbox_box within src/window.py, fully synchronized with the dynamic "Select All" / "Deselect All" button. Reason: Enables users to strip asterisk formatting markers automatically upon dragging and dropping Markdown or text files into ReadAloud.</li>
          <li>"Remove All" Tools Action (win.remove-all-tags): Added "Remove All" action item under the Tools submenu, backed by clean_all_tags() to strip round brackets, square brackets, pipes/tables, hashes, and stars in a single operation across either the current tab or all tabs. Reason: Delivers an instant, one-click all-in-one cleanup workflow for active documents and multi-tab sessions neatly organized under Tools.</li>
          <li>Keyboard Escape Dismissal for About Window: Added a local Gtk.ShortcutController to AboutReadAloudWindow binding the Escape key to close the window. Reason: Conforms to standard desktop dialog dismissal conventions.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Test Suite Expansion (210 Tests): Added comprehensive automated unit tests covering sub-tab stack structure, tab titles, changelog action routing, clean_star_symbols, clean_all_tags, remove-stars action, remove-all-tags action, menu hierarchy verification, and 5-option import dialog state toggles in tests/test_about_window.py, tests/test_text_tools.py, and tests/test_drag_and_drop.py, expanding test coverage to 210 automated unit tests. Reason: Guarantees stability and prevents regressions across text cleanup operations, menu actions, and dialog workflows.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Tag Stripping Pipeline Execution (apply_text_tag_stripping): Updated apply_text_tag_stripping() with the strip_stars parameter to chain markdown image, table/pipe, round bracket, square bracket, hash, and star cleaning in the optimal artifact-free order. Reason: Ensures all text cleaning operations execute cleanly without leaving detached exclamation marks, orphan punctuation, or irregular whitespace.</li>
          <li>Drag-and-Drop Placeholder Card Description: Updated the empty tab placeholder card bullet in src/window.ui to state "• Strip brackets, pipes, hashes, or stars on import". Reason: Accurately informs users of all available text cleaning capabilities.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.9): Updated application version to 1.8.9 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>GNOME Disks-Style Pill Header Switcher: Updated the About window titlebar to feature a linked segmented toggle button switcher [ About | Change Logs | Description | Credits | Legal ] centered in the headerbar. Reason: Creates a condensed, visually balanced, and intuitive desktop dialog matching modern GNOME applications.</li>
          <li>Import Dialog 5-Option Layout: Updated the document import dialog to present 5 neatly aligned tag-stripping checkboxes ("Remove ( ) round brackets and text", "Remove [ ] square brackets and text", "Remove | pipes and text", "Remove # hashes", "Remove * stars (asterisks)") under the "Select All" / "Deselect All" button. Reason: Delivers a harmonious, easily scannable layout that fits comfortably within modal alert boundaries.</li>
          <li>Burger Drop Down Menu "Remove All" Placement: Added "Remove All" item directly to the primary burger menu dropdown with clean separator line and inside the Tools submenu. Reason: Enhances accessibility by providing high-visibility access to full document cleanup directly from the main application menu.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.8" date="2026-10-10">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.8 introduces informative hover tooltip popups for the top-right Minimize, Maximize/Restore, and Close window controls, implements dynamic window state tracking that automatically updates the maximize button tooltip between "Maximize" and "Restore", adds titlebar close button tooltips across About and Change Logs dialogs, and expands automated regression test coverage, supported by 193 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unlabeled Window Control Buttons: Removed un-annotated headerbar window controls where hovering over the Minimize, Maximize, and Close buttons produced no tooltip popup. Reason: Window control buttons lacked descriptive hover tooltips, leaving users without visual confirmation or accessibility explanations of button functions.</li>
          <li>Static Maximize Control Labeling: Removed static title bar control state handling that did not distinguish between restored and maximized states. Reason: A static maximize label did not reflect the active window geometry or indicate that clicking the button while maximized will restore the window to its previous dimensions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Header Bar Window Controls Hover Tooltips: Added dynamic tooltip popups to the Minimize (_("Minimize")), Maximize (_("Maximize") / _("Restore")), and Close (_("Close")) buttons in _update_window_controls_tooltips within ReadAloudWindow. Reason: Delivers clear, standard tooltip popups on hover that explain exactly what each window control button does across all desktop environments.</li>
          <li>Reactive Window Maximize / Restore State Detection: Added connection to the window's notify::maximized GObject property signal and toggle_maximize_window handler to dynamically toggle the maximize button's tooltip between "Maximize" (when window is normal/restored) and "Restore" (when window is maximized). Reason: Provides accurate, real-time visual feedback indicating the action that will occur when clicking the button based on current window state.</li>
          <li>About Window Control Tooltip: Added close button tooltip assignment in configure_about_contents for Adw.AboutWindow navigation and subpages. Reason: Maintains consistent, accessible tooltip behavior across all secondary dialogs and windows.</li>
          <li>Window Controls Test Coverage: Added dedicated unit tests (test_window_controls_tooltips in tests/test_shortcuts.py and close button verification in tests/test_about_window.py), expanding the test suite to 193 automated tests. Reason: Validates tooltip initialization, dynamic text toggling between Maximize and Restore, and prevents regression in window control behavior.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Header Bar Initialization and Mapping Lifecycle: Updated ReadAloudWindow.__init__ and connected the window map signal to ensure window control tooltips are populated immediately upon widget hierarchy realization and refreshed upon window mapping. Reason: Ensures tooltips are consistently applied regardless of window manager decoration overrides or display server re-mapping events.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.8): Updated application version to 1.8.8 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Informative Window Control Popups on Hover: Updated the top-right headerbar controls so that hovering over the Minimize, Maximize/Restore, or Close buttons displays a native popup tooltip ("Minimize", "Maximize", "Restore", "Close"). Reason: Enhances visual clarity, accessibility, and desktop integration by clearly explaining the function of each button.</li>
          <li>About Window Close Button Tooltip: Updated the About window title bar controls so that hovering over the Close button displays "Close". Reason: Ensures visual consistency with main window controls.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.7" date="2026-10-07">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.7 resolves the word highlighting glitch across soft-wrapped lines and line breaks, introduces a "Select All" toggle button for the file import tag-stripping dialog, enables full tab name hover tooltips without premature truncation, expands em-dash and double-hyphen word tokenization, and adds comprehensive automated unit test coverage, supported by 192 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Logical Paragraph Line Iteration in Word Highlighting: Removed the logical paragraph line iteration in HighlightTextView.do_snapshot_layer that relied on newline delimiters (eol.forward_to_line_end() and cur.forward_line()). Reason: In GTK4 GtkTextView, soft-wrapped display lines within a paragraph do not contain newline (\n) characters; relying on logical line iterators caused line-end iterators to advance past the entire paragraph, producing inverted negative width calculations that truncated the highlight box to a tiny single-character sliver on the first line while leaving subsequent visual lines completely unhighlighted.</li>
          <li>Undifferentiated Em-Dash and Double-Hyphen Token Bundling: Removed the indiscriminate \S+ word tokenization in extract_sentences_and_words that treated words joined by closed em-dashes (—) or double-hyphens (--) as single inseparable tokens. Reason: Closed em-dashes and double-hyphens connect distinct words without whitespace; grouping them into one token forced speech synthesizer word boundary timings to span across multiple spoken words and cross over visual line break boundaries.</li>
          <li>Premature 24-Character Tab Title Truncation: Removed the artificial 24-character excerpt truncation (first_line[:24] + "…") in bubble._handle_retrieved_text and window.load_text_and_play. Reason: Hardcoding a 24-character slice permanently truncated the tab title string itself, preventing tooltips and hover popup boxes from ever displaying the complete tab title and cutting off phrases mid-word.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Display-Line Bounding Box Traversal (_get_highlight_rectangles): Added visual display line grouping in HighlightTextView that tracks character bounds and clusters them by visual line using vertical overlap (abs(loc.y - line_y) &lt;= max_height * 0.5) to compute precise bounding boxes (min_x, y, max_x - min_x, height) for each individual line touched by a highlighted span. Reason: Guarantees that any active word or phrase wrapping across one or multiple soft-wrapped visual display lines receives accurate, complete bounding boxes for every line it spans.</li>
          <li>Em-Dash and Double-Hyphen Word Tokenizer: Added regex sub-tokenization in extract_sentences_and_words that separates words connected by em-dashes (—) or double hyphens (--) into constituent words while keeping terminal punctuation attached and preserving exact character offsets matching original text slices. Reason: Synchronizes speech synthesizer word boundary events with individual spoken words so each word highlights independently and accurately during audio playback.</li>
          <li>"Select All" / "Deselect All" Import Dialog Toggle: Added a dedicated "Select All" toggle button to the file import dialog box (_create_tag_stripping_checkbox_box). Reason: Allows users to quickly toggle all 4 tag-stripping options (round brackets, square brackets, pipes, and hashes) on or off with a single click, eliminating the need to check each box individually.</li>
          <li>Explicit Tab Tooltip Synchronization: Added explicit page.set_tooltip(title) calls across create_new_tab, open_file, save_text_complete, _on_run_demo, and _prompt_empty_tab_import. Reason: Guarantees that hovering over any tab in AdwTabBar consistently displays a native tooltip popup containing the full tab title, even when the tab label on screen is constrained or ellipsized.</li>
          <li>Automated Regression Test Suite Expansion (192 Tests): Added unit tests covering line wrap highlight rectangles, em-dash word splitting, "Select All" toggle logic, full tab title retention, and tab tooltip synchronization in tests/test_highlight_and_language_tick.py, tests/test_drag_and_drop.py, tests/test_tab_system.py, and tests/test_bubble.py. Reason: Ensures stability, prevents regressions in highlight rendering and tab navigation, and validates import dialog interactions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Multiline Highlight Rendering in HighlightTextView.do_snapshot_layer: Updated snapshot rendering to draw individual 10px rounded padded rectangles across every visual display line segment returned by _get_highlight_rectangles, while retaining an O(1) fast-path for single-line words (loc1.y == loc2.y and loc2.x &gt; loc1.x). Reason: Delivers smooth, full-coverage highlight shapes across all lines for wrapped words or multi-word segments while preserving optimal rendering performance during real-time speech playback.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Checkbox State Tracking for Import Dialog: Updated _create_tag_stripping_checkbox_box to observe individual checkbutton toggles and dynamically update the button label between "Select All" (when any checkbox is unticked) and "Deselect All" (when all checkboxes are active). Reason: Provides clear visual feedback representing the current selection state at all times.</li>
          <li>Tab Header and Quick Read Title Preservation: Updated load_text_and_play and bubble._handle_retrieved_text to preserve the full first line of imported or selected text (with a 500-character sanity ceiling). Reason: Retains meaningful document context and full tab titles rather than cryptic truncated fragments.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.7): Maintained application version 1.8.7 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the bug fix release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Seamless Highlight Display Across Line Wraps: Updated active word highlighting so that when a word or phrase wraps across lines, each line displays a complete rounded yellow rectangle with 2x padding behind the text rather than a truncated box on the first line and black text on subsequent lines. Reason: Eliminates the visual highlight glitch where words wrapping at line breaks appeared cut off, partially highlighted, or illegible on dark themes.</li>
          <li>Complete Tab Name Popup on Hover: Updated the tab hover popup box in AdwTabBar so that it reveals the full, untruncated name of the tab instead of ending with an ellipsis (…). Reason: Enables users to instantly identify the full document or excerpt name by simply hovering over the tab, especially when tabs are narrow in multi-tab workflows.</li>
          <li>"Select All" Button in File Import Dialog: Added an aligned "Select All" button at the top of the tag-stripping checkbox list in Adw.AlertDialog with compact margins (margin_top=2, margin_bottom=2, spacing=3). Reason: Provides an accessible, well-proportioned layout that seamlessly integrates into both single-action and multi-action import dialogs without vertical clipping or awkward crowding.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.6" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.6 introduces full drag-and-drop file import for TXT and MD documents with an empty-tab visual guidance interface, introduces multi-select tag stripping check boxes on import allowing users to strip round brackets, square brackets, pipes, and hashes, adds a dedicated "Remove | Pipes" text cleanup tool with full Markdown table and delimiter row elimination, resolves Markdown table and image orphan exclamation mark artifacts upon import, and consolidates the Tools menu inside the primary Burger Menu, supported by 187 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Standalone Run Demo Headerbar Button: Removed the dedicated "Run Demo" dropdown button from the window headerbar. Reason: Reduces headerbar clutter, consolidates demo playback alongside other tools, and groups related voice tools logically under the Tools menu.</li>
          <li>Standalone Tools Headerbar Button (Top Left): Removed the standalone "Tools" dropdown menu button from the top-left section of the window headerbar. Reason: Eliminates visual clutter in the top-left toolbar, keeps the headerbar focused on primary file actions (Open and Save), and avoids redundant menus by centralizing text cleanup utilities and voice demos inside the primary Burger Menu.</li>
          <li>Direct Unchecked Empty Tab Import: Removed automatic immediate tab creation without prompt when dropping files into an empty document tab. Reason: Users dropping files into empty tabs had no opportunity to pre-process text or strip unwanted citations, brackets, metadata pipes, or heading hashes before populating the tab.</li>
          <li>Alternating Cell Consumption and Line-Break Bridging Regex: Removed the raw single-pass regex (<code>\|[^|]*\|</code> with DOTALL) that consumed shared column delimiter pipes and bridged across line breaks. Reason: Multi-column tables share boundary pipes between cells, and matching across newlines caused alternating cells across lines to be preserved and stitched together while leaving behind delimiter hyphens (---) and dangling pipe characters.</li>
          <li>Decoupled Image Bracket Stripping &amp; Orphan Exclamation Delimiters: Removed isolated bracket removal on Markdown image references that left leading exclamation marks (<code>!</code>) stranded on their own lines. Reason: Stripping only bracket pairs from <code>![image](url)</code> left behind disconnected <code>!</code> characters that speech synthesizers read aloud as "exclamation mark" and caused unsightly visual artifacts between paragraphs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Drag-and-Drop TXT &amp; MD File Ingestion: Added Gtk.DropTarget integration supporting drag-and-drop of TXT and MD text files directly into the application window. Reason: Allows users to quickly and naturally open documents by dropping files from their desktop or file manager.</li>
          <li>Empty Tab Drag-and-Drop Visual Guidance Card: Added an explanatory card centered in the editor canvas of empty tabs with an icon, title, format guidelines, and typing dismissal notice. Reason: Teaches new users how to import documents via drag-and-drop while an empty tab is active.</li>
          <li>Reactive Typing Dismissal of Placeholder: Implemented reactive buffer change detection that immediately hides the drag-and-drop guidance card when typing begins and restores it if the document is emptied. Reason: Maximizes clean, distraction-free writing space while keeping onboarding guidance available when needed.</li>
          <li>Incompatible File Format Validation &amp; Alert Dialog: Added strict file extension validation rejecting non-TXT and non-MD files (e.g., .pdf, .png, .py) with a native Adw.AlertDialog alert ("ReadAloud is only compatible with TXT or MD Files."). Reason: Protects against loading unreadable binary data or unsupported file formats into the speech synthesizer.</li>
          <li>Multi-Option Drop Dialog for Populated Tabs: When dropping files into a tab with existing text, prompts the user to choose between "Import into Existing Tab", "Create New Tabs per File", or "All into One New Tab" (with Cancel). Reason: Gives users explicit control over where dropped text is placed without accidentally overwriting existing work.</li>
          <li>Multi-Select Tag-Stripping Checkboxes on File Import: Added interactive check boxes to the file import dialogs (for both empty tabs and tabs with existing content) to remove round brackets, square brackets, pipes, and hashes. Reason: Empowers users to pre-process imported documents by stripping unwanted parenthetical notes, citation tags, markdown tables/pipes, or headers before text is loaded into tabs.</li>
          <li>Remove | Pipes Text Cleanup Tool: Added the "Remove | Pipes" cleanup tool (clean_pipe_brackets and win.remove-pipe-brackets) to the Tools menu, removing all text enclosed between pipe characters (and empty ||) while normalizing surrounding whitespace and punctuation. Reason: Allows users to remove metadata tags, wiki tables, and pipe-delimited fields so speech engines do not read unwanted pipe symbols or raw table syntax.</li>
          <li>Markdown Table Delimiter &amp; Block Detection: Added dedicated markdown table detection (is_table_separator) that identifies table separator rows (<code>| --- | --- |</code> or <code>--- | ---</code>) and scans upwards and downwards to mark all connected table header rows and data rows for removal. Reason: Markdown tables (such as Wikipedia infoboxes and structured documentation tables) contain pipe-delimited data that must be completely removed so speech engines do not read fragmented tabular syntax or table text.</li>
          <li>Full-Row Pipe Table Elimination: Added detection for lines beginning and ending with pipe characters (<code>| ... |</code>) to strip all single-column or multi-column table rows cleanly along with all text within them. Reason: Completely removes markdown table rows, infobox cards, and cell content without leaving stray characters or partial lines.</li>
          <li>Unified Markdown Image Stripping &amp; Orphan Exclamation Filter: Added pattern matching across bracket cleaners and import tag stripping to remove complete markdown image tags as unified units (<code>![alt](url)</code>), along with a line filter removing stranded exclamation mark lines (<code>!</code>). Reason: Completely eliminates leftover exclamation mark artifacts from imported Markdown articles while preserving legitimate sentence-ending punctuation.</li>
          <li>Preset Voice Demos Submenu inside Tools: Moved the preset voice demos (Demo 1 Jenny, Demo 2 Northern English Male, Demo 3 Joe) into a dedicated "Preset Voice Demos" subcategory inside the Tools menu. Reason: Creates a clean, centralized Tools hub containing both text cleanup tools and voice demonstration presets.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Centralized Burger Menu Tools Submenu: Consolidated all text cleanup tools (Remove Brackets, Pipes, Hashes) and Preset Voice Demos under the Tools submenu within the primary Burger Menu (≡). Reason: Provides a consistent, unified menu structure that keeps the application headerbar minimal and uncluttered.</li>
          <li>Markdown Table &amp; Image Artifact Cleanup: Updated clean_pipe_brackets(), clean_square_brackets(), clean_round_brackets(), and apply_text_tag_stripping() to eliminate markdown tables, image references, and orphan exclamation marks cleanly, leaving only surrounding text without residual artifacts like dashes (---), image exclamation marks (!), or glued words. Reason: Resolves visual and auditory artifacts where importing Markdown files left behind garbled table fragments or stray punctuation characters.</li>
          <li>Tag Stripping Pipeline Execution Order: Updated apply_text_tag_stripping() to execute image and table stripping before bracket and hash stripping. Reason: Strips markdown tables, images, and embedded URLs cleanly at the beginning of the pipeline so individual cleaners do not leave behind detached exclamation marks or partial image descriptions.</li>
          <li>Import Dialog Button Response Action Fix: Connected the Adw.AlertDialog import prompt directly to the "response" signal handler instead of dialog.choose(). Reason: Resolves an issue where dialog button clicks resulted in no action because dialog.choose() passes an asynchronous Gio.Task object rather than the response string.</li>
          <li>Text Cleanup Tool Tab Scope Dialog Support: Updated _prompt_and_apply_bracket_tool() and _apply_bracket_tool_to_view() to fully support all cleanup tools (round brackets, square brackets, pipes, and hashes). Reason: Provides a uniform dialog asking users whether to apply cleanup to the current tab or across all tabs.</li>
          <li>Atomic Undo Support for Text Cleaning Tools: Wrapped all bracket, pipe, and hash removal modifications in buffer.begin_user_action() and buffer.end_user_action(). Reason: Ensures all text cleanup operations can be instantly and safely reverted using Ctrl + Z undo.</li>
          <li>Expanded Automated Test Suite (187 Tests): Added comprehensive test suites in tests/test_text_tools.py and tests/test_drag_and_drop.py covering drag-and-drop ingestion, format validation, import tag stripping checkboxes, pipe bracket removal, markdown tables, markdown image syntax stripping, and orphan exclamation line elimination, bringing total passing tests to 187. Reason: Verifies stability, edge cases, and regression prevention across all new features.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.6): Maintained application version 1.8.6 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Adheres to semantic versioning standards for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Minimalist Streamlined Top-Left Headerbar: Removed the "Tools" dropdown button from the top-left area of the headerbar, leaving only the Open and Save buttons alongside the window title and tabs. Reason: Greatly simplifies the top-left window layout, creating a balanced, modern, and uncluttered toolbar aesthetic.</li>
          <li>Clean Post-Import Tab Text Display without Table or Image Artifacts: Updated imported tab rendering so that Markdown files with tables and images display only clean prose and headings, free from broken table borders, hyphens, dangling pipe characters, and floating exclamation marks. Reason: Delivers an aesthetically clean reading canvas in the text view without messy formatting artifacts.</li>
          <li>Centered Empty Tab Drag-and-Drop Guidance Card: Designed a modern centered card with a folder icon, bold title, bullet points, and subtitled hint on empty tab workspaces. Reason: Provides an attractive, informative visual empty-state that explains the drag-and-drop feature at a glance.</li>
          <li>Compact Multi-Select Checkboxes in Import Dialogs: Integrated 4 native Gtk.CheckButton checkboxes with clear labels into the Adw.AlertDialog extra child space. Reason: Delivers an intuitive, legible visual checklist for choosing tag stripping options upon file import.</li>
          <li>Updated Empty Tab Guidance Text: Refined the placeholder text to explicitly describe stripping brackets, pipes, or hashes on import. Reason: Informs users of the newly added tag-stripping capability directly within the interface.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.5" date="2026-10-03">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.5 introduces in-flight speech synthesis cancellation with a dedicated Cancel button on the loading HUD and Escape key shortcut, introduces a new "Tools" dropdown menu with brackets and hash symbol removal tools featuring tab-scope prompt dialogs and atomic undo support, and expands the Adjust Speed system to a 5-choice ladder by adding calibrated "Slow" and "Slower" settings across all 35 voice models, supported by 158 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Un-cancellable Background Speech Synthesis Loop: Removed the uninterruptible synthesis loop in Reader where Piper speech synthesis ran to completion regardless of user actions. Reason: Long document synthesis could not be aborted if started accidentally or with incorrect voice settings, locking the user out and tying up system CPU resources.</li>
          <li>3-Choice Speed System Limitation: Removed the restriction limiting speech rates to only Normal, Fast, and Super Fast. Reason: Many users found Normal too fast for dense or technical reading material, requiring slower, more relaxed playback tempos.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Speech Generation Cancellation &amp; Process Abort: Added full user cancellation capability to active audio synthesis in src/reader.py and src/window.py. Synthesis threads check for cancellation at sentence boundaries and immediately break out, halt generation, clean up partial temporary .wav files, dismiss the loading HUD, and re-enable window sensitivity. Reason: Gives users immediate control to stop unwanted or accidental synthesis operations instantly.</li>
          <li>Loading Indicator HUD Cancel Button &amp; Escape Key: Added a pill-shaped Cancel button (.loading-indicator-box .cancel-generation-button) to the loading HUD and bound the Escape key to abort generation. Reason: Delivers an intuitive, accessible visual and keyboard-driven mechanism to cancel audio generation at any moment.</li>
          <li>Tools Dropdown Menu in Header Bar: Added a dedicated Tools dropdown menu (GtkMenuButton id="tools_button") directly to the right of the Run Demo menu on the header bar, mirrored in the primary hamburger menu under Text Tools. Reason: Organizes text transformation and pre-reading cleanup utilities into a dedicated, easily accessible menu.</li>
          <li>Remove ( ) Round Brackets Tool: Added the "Remove ( ) Brackets" cleanup action, stripping round brackets and all enclosed text, including nested parentheses and multiline blocks, while normalizing surrounding whitespace and punctuation. Reason: Allows users to clean explanatory parenthetical remarks from articles and Wikipedia excerpts prior to speech synthesis.</li>
          <li>Remove [ ] Square Brackets Tool: Added the "Remove [ ] Brackets" cleanup action, stripping square brackets and enclosed citations (e.g., [1], [b], [citation needed]), while normalizing adjacent whitespace and punctuation. Reason: Strips distracting reference citation numbers and footnotes from copied encyclopedia texts so they are not read aloud.</li>
          <li>Remove # Hashes Tool: Added the "Remove # Hashes" cleanup action, stripping all # characters from text while collapsing multiple spaces and trimming line-leading indentation. Reason: Automatically converts Markdown headings (# Heading to Heading) and cleans hashtags and numeric hash markers so speech engines do not pronounce "hash" or "number sign".</li>
          <li>Text Tool Tab Scope Prompt Dialog: Added a modal Adw.AlertDialog when triggering any text cleanup tool, asking the user whether to apply the transformation to the Current Tab or All Tabs (or Cancel). Reason: Provides flexibility to clean a single active document or perform batch cleanup across all open tabs simultaneously.</li>
          <li>Atomic Reversible Buffer Edits (Undo Support): Wrapped all text tool transformations in begin_user_action() and end_user_action(). Reason: Enables users to instantly revert any bracket or hash removal using standard Ctrl + Z undo.</li>
          <li>"Slow" and "Slower" Speed Options: Expanded the Adjust Speed dropdown from 3 choices to 5 discrete choices: Slower, Slow, Normal, Fast, and Super Fast. Reason: Provides calibrated, slower tempo choices below Normal for relaxed listening and comprehension of complex texts.</li>
          <li>35-Voice Model Slow &amp; Slower Speed Calibration: Calibrated Slow as Normal minus 0.1 and Slower as Normal minus 0.2 across all 35 British and American English Piper voice models in VOICE_MODEL_SPEEDS. Reason: Retains model-specific cadence adjustments tailored to each voice's natural delivery.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Speed Playback Settings Breakdown by Voice Model:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>en_GB-alan-low: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_GB-alan-medium: Slower: 0.8 | Slow: 0.9 | Normal: 1.0 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-alba-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-aru-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-cori-high: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-cori-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-jenny_dioco-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_GB-northern_english_male-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_GB-semaine-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-southern_english_female-low: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_GB-vctk-medium: Slower: 0.2 | Slow: 0.3 | Normal: 0.4 | Fast: 0.9 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_US-amy-low: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-amy-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-arctic-medium: Slower: 0.4 | Slow: 0.5 | Normal: 0.6 | Fast: 0.9 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_US-bryce-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-danny-low: Slower: 0.4 | Slow: 0.5 | Normal: 0.6 | Fast: 0.9 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_US-hfc_female-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-hfc_male-medium: Slower: 0.7 | Slow: 0.8 | Normal: 0.9 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.5</li>
          <li>en_US-joe-medium: Slower: 0.7 | Slow: 0.8 | Normal: 0.9 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.5</li>
          <li>en_US-john-medium: Slower: 0.8 | Slow: 0.9 | Normal: 1.0 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-kathleen-low: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-kristin-medium: Slower: 0.8 | Slow: 0.9 | Normal: 1.0 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-kusal-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-l2arctic-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-lessac-high: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-lessac-low: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-lessac-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-libritts-high: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-libritts_r-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ljspeech-high: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-ljspeech-medium: Slower: 0.6 | Slow: 0.7 | Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-norman-medium: Slower: 0.4 | Slow: 0.5 | Normal: 0.6 | Fast: 0.9 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-high: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-low: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-medium: Slower: 0.5 | Slow: 0.6 | Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Speed Dropdown UI &amp; Default Selection: Updated GtkDropDown in src/window.ui to list Slower, Slow, Normal, Fast, and Super Fast, with Normal selected by default (index 2). Reason: Aligns the UI options with the expanded 5-choice speed ladder while keeping Normal as the default baseline.</li>
          <li>Speed Keyboard Navigation (Ctrl + Up and Ctrl + Down): Updated increase_speed() and decrease_speed() to cycle across all 5 discrete choices with bounds clamping. Reason: Provides seamless keyboard stepping from Slower through Super Fast.</li>
          <li>Batch Audio Export Cancellation Handling: Updated _batch_export_tabs_audio() in src/window.py to monitor cancellation flags. Reason: Cancelling during multi-tab batch export stops subsequent tab processing immediately and closes the progress dialog.</li>
          <li>Expanded Test Suite (158 Tests): Added tests/test_generation_cancellation.py and expanded tests/test_speed_dropdown.py and tests/test_text_tools.py to bring total automated unit tests to 158. Reason: Ensures robust test coverage for cancellation, 5-choice speed mappings, and text cleanup tools.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.5): Updated application version from 1.8.4 to 1.8.5 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Reflects the new release adhering to semantic versioning.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pill-Shaped Cancel Button on Translucent HUD: Designed a sleek pill-shaped Cancel button on the dark translucent HUD with hover and active states matching Libadwaita styling. Reason: Provides a visually appealing, prominent abort control that integrates into the existing loading indicator.</li>
          <li>New Tools Dropdown on Header Bar: Positioned the "Tools ▾" button immediately adjacent to "Run Demo ▾". Reason: Creates a balanced, organized headerbar layout with clear visual affordances for text manipulation.</li>
          <li>5-Row Speed Popover with Active Selection Tick: The speed dropdown popover now presents all 5 options in vertical progression with an active checkmark (✓) dynamically reflecting the selected speed. Reason: Offers clear visual feedback of the selected speaking rate.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.4" date="2026-10-01">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.4 simplifies speech rate adjustment by replacing the continuous float slider with a streamlined 3-choice dropdown (Normal, Fast, Super Fast), calibrated across all 35 voice models with active selection tick marks and automatic viewport centering when opening dropdown lists, supported by 136 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Continuous 0.1–2.0 Float Speed Slider and Popover: Removed the GtkScale speed adjustment slider and popover menu button from the bottom toolbar in src/window.ui and src/window.py. Reason: The continuous decimal slider was imprecise and cumbersome to adjust, whereas voices require distinct, voice-model-tailored speaking tempos for optimal clarity.</li>
          <li>Speed Multiplier Label and Template Bindings: Removed label_2 (speed multiplier text display) and adjustment_2 Gtk.Template.Child bindings from the window class in src/window.py. Reason: Obsolete template child bindings were retired in favor of the standardized GtkDropDown component with backward-compatible proxy methods.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Simplified 3-Choice Speed Dropdown: Added a dedicated speed dropdown (GtkDropDown id="speed_chooser") on the bottom toolbar offering three discrete, accessible settings: Normal, Fast, and Super Fast. Reason: Simplifies user experience by providing clear, natural, and immediate tempo selections without decimal guesswork.</li>
          <li>35-Voice Model Speed Conversion Engine: Implemented VOICE_MODEL_SPEEDS dictionary and get_speed_for_voice() in src/window.py mapping all 35 British and American English Piper voice models to calibrated speed floats for Normal, Fast, and Super Fast modes. Reason: Accounts for inherent cadence variations across different voice models to deliver consistent, natural pacing for every voice.</li>
          <li>Dropdown Selection Tickmark for Speed: Added active selection checkmarks (✓) next to the chosen speed option in the speed popup list via _setup_dropdown_excerpt(). Reason: Delivers immediate visual confirmation of the currently active speed setting consistent with the language and voice choosers.</li>
          <li>Automatic Popover Centering on Active Ticked Choice: Implemented automatic scrolling and vertical centering on notify::visible in _setup_dropdown_excerpt(), ensuring that when a dropdown opens, the active ticked item (such as Ryan Voice further down the list) is immediately centered and visible. Reason: Eliminates the need for manual scrolling to locate the currently selected option in long lists.</li>
          <li>Automated Speed Dropdown &amp; Viewport Centering Test Suite: Added tests/test_speed_dropdown.py containing comprehensive tests for all 35 voice model speeds, helper resolution, dropdown UI items, get_value/set_value compatibility, popup checkmarks, keyboard cycling, and automatic popover scrolling, expanding the suite to 136 passing tests. Reason: Protects against regressions in speed mappings, UI dropdown operations, and keyboard navigation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Speed Playback Settings Breakdown by Voice Model:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>en_GB-alan-low: Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_GB-alan-medium: Normal: 1.0 | Fast: 1.2 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_GB-alba-medium: Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
