          <li>en_US-lessac-high: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-lessac-low: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-lessac-medium: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-libritts-high: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-libritts_r-medium: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ljspeech-high: Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-ljspeech-medium: Normal: 0.8 | Fast: 1.1 | Super Fast: 1.4</li>
          <li>en_US-norman-medium: Normal: 0.6 | Fast: 0.9 | Super Fast: 1.2</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-high: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-low: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
          <li>en_US-ryan-medium: Normal: 0.7 | Fast: 1.0 | Super Fast: 1.3</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Speed Keyboard Shortcuts (Ctrl + Up and Ctrl + Down): Updated increase_speed() and decrease_speed() to cycle smoothly between Normal (0), Fast (1), and Super Fast (2) with bounds clamping while preserving fallback compatibility. Reason: Aligns keyboard shortcuts with the simplified 3-choice speed system without breaking existing accelerator keybindings.</li>
          <li>Playback Pipeline and Dynamic Voice Switching: Updated playback initialization and toggle_pause() settings change detection to resolve current speed floats dynamically from the active speed mode and selected voice. Reason: Guarantees seamless audio generation and cached playback consistency when switching voices or speed modes.</li>
          <li>Documentation and Readme References: Updated README.md and app metainfo descriptions to reflect the simplified 3-choice speed dropdown and discrete keyboard navigation. Reason: Maintains accurate, user-facing feature documentation.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.4): Updated application version from 1.8.3 to 1.8.4 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Reflects the new release adhering to semantic versioning.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Cohesive Bottom Toolbar with Speed Dropdown Button: Styled the new speed dropdown button with the speed symbolic gauge icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.speed-symbolic) and active mode text alongside the dropdown indicator ([icon] Normal ▾), perfectly harmonizing with the language and voice choosers. Reason: Establishes a clean, unified visual design language across all bottom toolbar controls.</li>
          <li>Instant Centered Viewport on Dropdown Open: Dropdown popovers now automatically position the selected choice with its checkmark directly in the middle of the popup viewport upon opening. Reason: Enhances visual ergonomics and usability by eliminating tedious searching and scrolling.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.3" date="2026-09-29">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.3 expands the dynamic editor font zoom ceiling from 300% to 1000%, delivering an ultra-accessible 10× text magnification range with responsive word wrapping, continuous keyboard and mouse wheel scaling, and full settings persistence, supported by 129 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>300% Maximum Font Zoom Ceiling: Removed the hardcoded 300% maximum font size limitation (min(int(percentage), 300)) in src/window.py. Reason: Users with visual impairments, large high-DPI displays (such as 4K and 8K monitors), or room-scale distance reading environments were constrained by the 300% ceiling, which restricted large-format text magnification.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>1000% Ultra-Accessible Dynamic Font Scaling: Added support for scaling editor text up to 1000% (10× baseline magnification) in set_text_zoom(), enabling seamless zoom traversal from 70% to 1000% in 10% increments via Ctrl +, Ctrl -, Ctrl 0, and Ctrl + Mouse Scroll Wheel. Reason: Provides unrestricted accessibility and legibility across all display form factors and viewing distances without text clipping or layout breakdown.</li>
          <li>Text Zoom Range &amp; Shortcut Automated Unit Test: Added test_text_zoom_levels_and_shortcuts in tests/test_shortcuts.py, validating zoom scaling up to 1000%, lower bound clamping at 70%, out-of-range value handling, and Ctrl + / Ctrl - / Ctrl 0 keyboard shortcuts, expanding the test suite to 129 passing tests. Reason: Prevents future regressions in zoom limits, keyboard shortcuts, and CSS dynamic styling.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Documentation of Extended Zoom Range: Updated README.md Dynamic Text Zoom specification from 70%–300% to 70%–1000%. Reason: Keeps user-facing feature documentation and shortcut references accurate and up to date.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.3): Updated application version from 1.8.2 to 1.8.3 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Reflects the new release adhering to semantic versioning.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>High-Magnification Typography Rendering: Editor text can now expand up to 1000% scale while maintaining crisp vector glyph rendering, balanced line heights, and responsive soft-wrapping. Reason: Allows comfortable reading of oversized text from across the room or on large television/presentation screens without horizontal overflow.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.2" date="2026-09-26">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.2 introduces native title bar window controls with Minimize and Maximize/Restore buttons positioned immediately after the primary burger menu, native window manager integration with keyboard shortcuts and application actions, and a comprehensive AI engineering attribution and open-source licensing acknowledgment in the Application Description window, backed by 128 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>GNOME Title Bar Single-Close Default Limitation (:close): Removed reliance on GNOME/Libadwaita's standard single-button title bar layout (:close) by explicitly defining and enforcing :minimize,maximize,close in both src/window.ui and src/window.py. Reason: In default GNOME desktop environments, title buttons are restricted solely to the close button, preventing users from directly minimizing or maximizing the application window via header bar controls without external system-level configuration tweaks.</li>
          <li>Omission of AI Tooling &amp; Open-Source Engineering Attribution: Removed the undocumented gap regarding AI tool usage and engineering ownership in the application description. Reason: Transparent attribution ensures users and open-source contributors understand the architecture and review rigor behind AI-accelerated development while reaffirming full ownership of technical decisions and copyleft reciprocal obligations under the GNU General Public License v3.0.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Top-Right Minimize and Maximize Header Bar Controls: Added dedicated Minimize (window-minimize-symbolic / —) and Maximize/Restore (window-maximize-symbolic / □) title buttons placed immediately after the primary menu (burger) button on the right side of AdwHeaderBar. Reason: Provides users across all desktop environments (GNOME, KDE Plasma, XFCE, Windows) with immediate, intuitive, and standard window management controls.</li>
          <li>Application Window Management Actions (win.minimize &amp; win.toggle-maximize): Added minimize_window() calling self.minimize() and toggle_maximize_window() toggling between self.maximize() and self.unmaximize(), exposing them as win.minimize and win.toggle-maximize Gio actions on ReadAloudWindow. Reason: Enables robust programmatic control of window state accessible via actions, menus, and keyboard shortcuts.</li>
          <li>Primary Menu Window Control Items: Added "Minimize Window" and "Maximize Window" action items into the primary burger menu dropdown (primary_menu). Reason: Allows accessibility and menu-driven window control for users who prefer navigation via application menus or keyboard menu navigation.</li>
          <li>F11 Maximize / Restore Keyboard Shortcut: Added the F11 key binding in _on_window_key_pressed to toggle window maximization, fully documented in the Keyboard Shortcuts help overlay (src/gtk/help-overlay.ui). Reason: Conforms to standard desktop conventions for fullscreen/maximize toggling with a single dedicated key press.</li>
          <li>AI Acceleration &amp; Core Architecture Attribution in Application Description: Added the dedicated engineering acknowledgment paragraph verbatim into APP_DESCRIPTION displayed in the Application Description page of the About window. Reason: Clearly states that while AI tools such as Anti-gravity and Claude were leveraged to accelerate software development, core architecture, rigorous code reviews, technical trade-offs, and GPL v3 open-source compliance remain entirely owned by the author.</li>
          <li>Window Controls &amp; Description Test Suite Expansion: Added test cases in tests/test_shortcuts.py (test_header_bar_decoration_layout, test_minimize_and_maximize_actions, test_f11_shortcut_toggles_maximize) and tests/test_about_window.py (Anti-gravity, Claude, and open-source terms), expanding test suite coverage to 128 passing tests. Reason: Prevents regressions in window management behavior, headerbar decoration layouts, shortcuts, and metadata integrity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Header Bar Decoration Enforcement on Window Initialization: Updated ReadAloudWindow.__init__ to explicitly bind header_bar and call self.header_bar.set_decoration_layout(":minimize,maximize,close"). Reason: Ensures the window control layout is strictly maintained at runtime regardless of theme overrides or desktop settings daemon interference.</li>
          <li>About Dialog Description &amp; Test Verification: Updated APP_DESCRIPTION in src/main.py and tests/test_about_window.py to seamlessly integrate the new third paragraph while preserving quality level and multi-speaker model documentation. Reason: Maintains cohesive visual formatting, readable typography, and complete test verification in the details subpage.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.2): Updated application version from 1.8.1 to 1.8.2 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, build_windows/win_entrypoint.py, and CI workflows (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml). Reason: Conforms to semantic versioning for the new release.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Top-Right Title Bar Controls Layout: The top-right corner of the window now cleanly renders the Burger Menu button followed in sequence by the Minimize button (—), Maximize/Restore button (□), and Close button (✕). Reason: Establishes a balanced, familiar window title bar interface consistent with modern multi-platform desktop user experiences.</li>
          <li>Application Description Window Typography Flow: The Application Description subpage in the About ReadAloud window features the newly added engineering paragraph positioned with consistent paragraph spacing directly after the offline privacy guarantee. Reason: Enhances transparency and readability within the Libadwaita clamp container without cramping adjacent paragraphs or causing visual overflow.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.1" date="2026-09-25">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8.1 introduces vertical viewport center-alignment during speech playback, completely eliminates text jumping and micro-flickering across words on the same line, adds dynamic tail-padding for end-of-document centering, and introduces an automated standalone Microsoft Windows executable packaging and installer toolchain, supported by 125 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Bottom-Pinned Viewport Threshold Scrolling (use_align=False): Removed the minimum-distance viewport threshold auto-scrolling (use_align=False, within_margin=0.1) in src/window.py. Reason: Only scrolling when text reached the bottom 10% of the viewport pinned the actively spoken text line directly against the bottom toolbar, cutting off upcoming lines and causing eye strain.</li>
          <li>Conflicting Immediate Adjustment Snaps (vadj.set_value): Removed manual programmatic adjustment setting (vadj.set_value(clamped_val)) from _highlight_word. Reason: Manually setting the adjustment on every single highlighted word abruptly interrupted GTK's native smooth-scroll interpolation, fighting with the target baseline and causing rapid 5-pixel vertical saw-tooth vibration and flickering on every word during playback.</li>
          <li>Redundant Per-Word Scrolling on Identical Visual Lines: Removed unconditional scrolling invocation on every word highlight event. Reason: Re-triggering scroll physics across words on the exact same visual line caused micro-jitter and continuous layout recalculation; keeping the viewport stationary while traversing words on a line provides a stable, flicker-free reading experience.</li>
          <li>Restricted 12px Editor Bottom Margin: Removed the static 12px bottom text margin in editor tabs. Reason: Without sufficient padding at the end of the text buffer, the viewport ran out of scrollable room, trapping the final paragraphs at the bottom of the window and preventing them from reaching the center of the screen.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>True Vertical Center Auto-Scroller (yalign=0.5): Added true vertical center scrolling using GTK's native scroll_to_iter alignment (within_margin=0.0, use_align=True, xalign=0.0, yalign=0.5), keeping the active highlighted word line dead-center in the window during playback. Reason: Guarantees that the active line is always centered 50% from top and bottom, giving readers balanced view of preceding context and upcoming lines ahead.</li>
          <li>Dynamic End-of-Document Bottom Margin Expansion: Added dynamic bottom margin calculation (desired_bottom_margin = max(350, int(page_size * 0.5))) on the editor's text view. Reason: Ensures that regardless of window height, the document tail always has at least half a viewport of trailing space, enabling the very last sentence of any document to scroll to the exact vertical center of the screen without toolbar collision.</li>
          <li>Visual Line &amp; Paragraph Change Detection: Added dual tracking of visual line coordinates (self._last_scrolled_line_y) and buffer line indices (self._last_scrolled_line_idx), with automated off-screen detection and force_scroll override for seeking. Reason: Guarantees that scrolling only engages when speech transitions across visual lines (hard newlines or soft wraps) or during navigation, keeping the viewport completely rock-solid and still while reading words on the same line.</li>
          <li>Standalone Microsoft Windows Executable &amp; Installer Toolchain: Added Windows packaging suite with PyInstaller specification (build_windows/ReadAloud.spec), entry point wrapper (build_windows/win_entrypoint.py), Windows dependencies (requirements-windows.txt), Inno Setup compiler script (build_windows/installer.iss), and GitHub Actions CI workflow (.github/workflows/build-windows.yml) generating portable zip and setup installer executables. Reason: Enables native standalone execution and distribution of ReadAloud on 64-bit Microsoft Windows without requiring separate MSYS2 or Linux installations.</li>
          <li>Same-Line Playback Stability Automated Test: Added test_highlight_word_no_jumping_on_same_line in tests/test_highlight_and_language_tick.py, expanding the automated unit test suite to 125 passing tests. Reason: Verifies programmatically that multiple word highlights on the same line do not trigger spurious scroll calls, preventing regressions in reading stability.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Smooth Viewport Interpolation in _highlight_word: Updated auto-scrolling to rely exclusively on GTK4's native smooth-scrolling ease-out curves without external adjustment overrides. Reason: Delivers fluid, organic vertical transitions when advancing from one line to the next with zero direction reversals or jitter.</li>
          <li>Highlight State Invalidation on Seek &amp; Tab Switch: Updated _clear_highlight() and tab selection callbacks to reset _last_scrolled_line_y = None and _last_scrolled_line_idx = None. Reason: Ensures that stopping, seeking, or switching documents immediately re-centers the new active word on the first speech tick.</li>
          <li>Application Version Increment (1.8.1): Updated application version from 1.8 to 1.8.1 across meson.build, src/main.py, data/im.zackarious.ReadAloud.metainfo.xml.in, README.md, build_windows/installer.iss, and CI workflows. Reason: Reflects the new release adhering to semantic versioning.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Centered Active Reading Viewport: The currently spoken line remains positioned at the vertical midpoint of the display, with ample breathing room above and below. Reason: Dramatically reduces eye fatigue and eliminates obstruction from the bottom action toolbar.</li>
          <li>Rock-Solid In-Line Word Traversal: Highlighted words advance across the active line with zero vertical jumping, oscillation, or stutter. Reason: Creates a pleasant, calm reading environment where the text stays stationary under the reader's gaze.</li>
          <li>Smooth Eased Line Transitions: When speech moves to a new line, the viewport smoothly glides downward in a single fluid motion. Reason: Replaces abrupt jumping with a polished, professional animation.</li>
          <li>Generous Bottom Clearance for Tail Sentences: The bottom padding extends dynamically below the text, lifting the final lines off the window edge. Reason: Prevents the last sentence from getting cut in half or obscured behind playback controls.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8" date="2026-09-17">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.8 introduces a redesigned geometric plus-style cross layout for the Quick Listener desktop companion widget, permanently locking the central Play/Pause button at its exact on-screen position across both compact and expanded states, smooth organic outward and inward morphology animations, unified outer perimeter styling with inner border elimination, 100% transparent click-through corner cutouts via dynamic compositor input regions, persistent rewind and forward controls with GTK4 GSK render cache invalidation, and full Wayland/X11 compatibility, supported by 122 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Asymmetric Window Expansion and Positional Drift (B3 to C5): Removed the dynamic top-left resizing mechanism that resized the window from 72×72px down-and-right to 216×216px, which previously shifted the central Play/Pause button across the user's desktop (e.g. from grid position B3 to C5). Reason: Shifting the button position disoriented users and moved the button away from the pointer during hover expansion; anchoring the center button at (108, 108) within a constant 216×216px transparent canvas ensures the Play/Pause button remains completely stationary on screen while controls emerge around it.</li>
          <li>Inner Border Lines Around Center Play/Pause Button: Removed interior white borders and separate bounding box strokes around the central Play/Pause button. Reason: Interior dividing lines made the layout appear cluttered and fragmented; drawing a unified continuous outer perimeter contour gives the plus layout a sleek, seamless, cohesive aesthetic.</li>
          <li>Opaque and Pointer-Blocking Corner Bounding Box: Removed opaque background fills and pointer-intercepting canvas areas in the four corner cutouts surrounding the plus shape. Reason: A solid rectangular bounding box blocked user interaction with desktop windows underneath; integrating Gdk.Surface.set_input_region guarantees mouse clicks and scroll events in transparent corners pass straight through to underlying applications.</li>
          <li>Stale Opacity Guards in Middle Row Snapshotting: Removed local opacity guards (if op &gt; 0.005:) and decoupled progress state in MiddleRowBox. Reason: In GTK4, container render node caching (GSK) caused the Rewind 15s and Fast Forward 15s buttons to intermittently vanish when local progress lagged behind the parent container; deriving progress directly from PlusBubbleBox and invalidating render nodes guarantees all controls persist reliably.</li>
          <li>Full Circular Expansion Profile: Removed expanding into a solid 216×216px circular disc (border-radius: 50%) when hovering over the Play/Pause button. Reason: Replaced with an ergonomic plus-style cross layout where arms branch out directionally toward each corresponding button, minimizing desktop footprint while providing distinct directional targets.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Center-Locked Play/Pause Position Anchor: Added a fixed-center coordinate architecture (108, 108) on a constant 216×216px transparent canvas, keeping the central Play/Pause button permanently anchored at its exact on-screen position (e.g. B3) in both compact circular mode and expanded plus mode. Reason: Completely eliminates positional drift upon expansion while remaining 100% compatible with Wayland compositors (which strictly prohibit client-side window repositioning).</li>
          <li>Dynamic Input Region Pass-Through via Gdk.Surface.set_input_region: Added dynamic cairo.Region masking in _update_input_region that restricts pointer events to the 72×72px circular bounds in compact mode and the horizontal/vertical cross arms in expanded mode. Reason: Allows clicks and gestures in the four corner cutouts and outer canvas area to pass directly through to desktop windows underneath without intercepting user input.</li>
          <li>Directional Symmetrical Plus Expansion Layout: Added directional outward expansion where secondary controls emerge symmetrically around the stationary Play/Pause button: Export CD (Top), Stop Playback (Bottom), Rewind 15s (Left), and Fast Forward 15s (Right). Reason: Provides an intuitive, natural spatial layout where the user can access navigation and export options without their cursor losing contact with the primary playback button.</li>
          <li>Smooth Outward (260ms) and Inward (200ms) Plus Morphology Animations: Added tick-driven easing animations (ep = p²(3 - 2p)) in PlusBubbleBox that smoothly stretch the circle into the plus shape while translating sub-buttons outward from the center into their respective positions. Reason: Creates an organic, polished transition where controls bloom smoothly from behind the Play/Pause button rather than appearing abruptly.</li>
          <li>Unified Cairo Perimeter Path Construction: Added dynamic vector path tracing in PlusBubbleBox.do_snapshot using four rounded semicircular arm caps and inner right-angle corners with a single continuous 2.5px white border stroke (#ffffff). Reason: Produces a clean, vector-sharp plus shape border with zero interior dividing lines across any scaling factor or display DPI.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>GSK Render Node Synchronization for Rewind and Fast Forward Icons: Updated MiddleRowBox.do_snapshot to derive animation progress directly from its parent PlusBubbleBox, bypassed opacity/translation transforms when expanded, and explicitly invalidated redraw passes with self.middle_box.queue_draw(). Reason: Resolves an issue where GTK4's Scene Graph (GSK) reused stale cached render nodes with zero opacity, causing Rewind and Fast Forward buttons to intermittently disappear.</li>
          <li>Euclidean Hit-Testing and Motion Tracking for (108, 108) Center: Updated _is_point_in_plus, _get_button_at_pos, and pointer motion tracking to calculate Euclidean distances from the new (108, 108) center and cross arms. Reason: Guarantees accurate button activation, hover highlights, and drag detection across the fixed 216×216px canvas in both compact circle mode and expanded plus mode.</li>
          <li>Quick Listener Collapse Finalizer: Updated _finish_collapse to maintain the 216×216px transparent window size and re-apply the compact 72×72px input mask rather than resizing top-level window geometry. Reason: Prevents window manager origin jumping and maintains exact desktop placement when collapsing back to the compact circular bubble.</li>
          <li>Automated Test Suite Expansion (122 Tests Passing): Updated tests/test_bubble.py to validate the (108, 108) center anchor, plus arm hit-testing, corner cutout pass-through, expanded button persistence, and CSS transparency. Reason: Ensures complete test coverage and prevents future regressions across all Quick Listener interaction flows.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Geometric Plus-Style Cross Silhouette: The Quick Listener expands into a distinct plus-shaped cross with four rounded arms extending 72px from the center, replacing the previous solid circular disc. Reason: Creates an iconic, visually uncluttered silhouette that clearly defines the 5 interactive control regions.</li>
          <li>Seamless Unified Outer Border with Zero Inner Lines: The plus shape features a single continuous 2.5px solid white border (#ffffff) around its outer perimeter, with all interior borders around the play/pause button removed. Reason: Establishes a minimalist, cohesive appearance without distracting interior dividing lines.</li>
          <li>100% Transparent Pass-Through Corner Cutouts: The four corner quadrants between the plus arms are rendered completely transparent with zero dark overlay or bounding box shading. Reason: Blends naturally with any wallpaper or application window underneath without blocking visual content.</li>
          <li>Smooth Outward Emerge Transition for Sub-Buttons: Sub-button icons slide outward from behind the center Play/Pause button into their final positions while fading in from opacity 0 to 1 during expansion. Reason: Delivers fluid visual choreography that makes the controls feel as though they are blooming directly from the primary button.</li>
          <li>Center-Anchored Visual Position Stability: The Play/Pause button remains visually fixed at the exact same screen coordinates throughout hover expansion and collapse. Reason: Eliminates jarring visual jumping and ensures complete visual consistency for the user.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.7" date="2026-09-16">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.7 introduces interactive playback controls directly onto the floating Quick Listener companion widget, including a dynamic 5-button cross (D-pad) layout revealing export audio (single or multi-tab), 15-second rewind, pause/resume, stop, and fast-forward controls when hovering over the active play or pause icon, a 1.5-second anti-flicker leave delay, paused seeking with word scrolling and automatic resume, instant pause/resume toggling, all styled in signature golden yellow matching the ReadAloud brand identity with 3D flip transitions, tactile bounce feedback, precision word highlight synchronization during seeks, contextual right-click menu options, and bi-directional playback synchronization, supported by 117 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Abrupt 150ms Leave Timeout on Quick Listener: Removed the aggressive 150ms collapse timeout triggered when the mouse pointer leaves the expanded Quick Listener bubble. Reason: A 150ms timeout caused severe visual flickering and abrupt accidental collapse whenever the user's cursor brushed against the border or briefly moved between controls; replacing it with a 1.5-second debounce delay ensures a smooth, forgiving user experience.</li>
          <li>Horizontal 288×72px Capsule Hover Layout: Removed the linear 4-button horizontal strip container (288×72px) for expanded Quick Listener controls. Reason: Replaced with a balanced 216×216px 5-button cross (D-pad) arrangement that places Stop underneath Pause, Rewind to the left, Forward to the right, and adds an Export Audio button directly above Pause for intuitive directional navigation.</li>
          <li>Static Single-Action Quick Listener Click Behavior: Removed unconditional invocation of clipboard text capture on every bubble left-click regardless of whether audio was already playing. Reason: Clicking the bubble during active listening previously interrupted playback and redundantly opened new document tabs; replacing this with contextual playback awareness allows users to pause, resume, and seek active audio smoothly.</li>
          <li>Static Speaker Icon Display During Audio Playback: Removed displaying the static speaker megaphone icon while audio is actively playing or paused. Reason: A static icon offered no visual indication of ongoing playback or available interactive controls; dynamically switching to pause and play icons gives immediate visual confirmation of audio status.</li>
          <li>White Monochrome Icon Styling in Quick Listener: Removed the plain white icon color (color: #ffffff) from the listener bubble stylesheet. Reason: Plain white icons lacked visual connection with the application's signature golden yellow identity; styling all icons in matching bright yellow (#fee14d) delivers striking high-contrast vibrancy against the black circular bubble background.</li>
          <li>Generic Desktop Seek Symbolic Icons: Removed reliance on generic desktop seek icon names (media-seek-backward-symbolic and media-seek-forward-symbolic). Reason: Desktop icon themes frequently override these icons with hardcoded grey fills (#dedede), generic double-arrows, or missing glyphs under Flatpak, failing to reflect the signature golden yellow styling or dedicated 15-second skip action.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>1.5-Second Anti-Flicker Hover Leave Debounce Delay: Added a 1.5-second (1500ms) delay before collapsing the Quick Listener bubble when the pointer leaves the widget. If the user moves back into the bubble within 1.5 seconds, the collapse timer is cancelled immediately and controls remain smoothly expanded. Reason: Stops aggressive visual flickering and prevents accidental collapse when users accidentally move the mouse over or away from the play/pause and navigation buttons.</li>
          <li>Paused Seeking with Auto-Resume Playback: Added automatic audio playback resumption when clicking the Rewind 15s or Fast Forward 15s buttons while playback is paused, alongside immediate word highlight updating and auto-scrolling to the new speech position. Reason: Allows users to quickly skip to a new passage while paused and immediately continue listening without needing a second click on the Play button.</li>
          <li>Quick Listener Export Audio Integration: Added dedicated Export Audio button (export_box) located directly above the Pause icon in the top slot of the cross layout, using the bundled CD vinyl icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.cd). Clicking it invokes main_window.save_audio_dialog(), allowing users to export the current tab or batch export all open tabs directly from the desktop companion widget without opening or refocusing the main window. Added corresponding "Export Audio" (bubble.export) action to the right-click context menu. Reason: Empowers users to save synthesized audio files effortlessly from anywhere on the desktop while listening to speech.</li>
          <li>Quick Listener 5-Button Cross (D-pad) Expansion: Added dynamic expansion from a 72×72px compact circle into a 216×216px circular cross layout when hovering over the Pause or Play icon during an active audio session, revealing Export Audio (Top), Rewind 15s (Left), Pause/Play (Center), Fast Forward 15s (Right), and Stop Playback (Bottom). Reason: Provides balanced, ergonomic directional navigation that groups all core playback and export actions around the central button.</li>
          <li>Quick Listener Complete Playback Stop Functionality: Added dedicated Stop playback button (stop_box, im.zackarious.ReadAloud.stop-symbolic) underneath the Pause icon and in the right-click popover menu. Clicking Stop halts audio immediately, removes text highlight markers, resets playback state, and flips the Quick Listener bubble back to its compact 72×72px circular profile with the yellow speaker application icon. Reason: Allows users to fully terminate an audio reading session directly from the desktop companion widget without opening or refocusing the main application window.</li>
          <li>Dedicated 15-Second Rewind &amp; Fast-Forward Action Icons: Added custom bundled action icons (im.zackarious.ReadAloud.rewind-15-symbolic and im.zackarious.ReadAloud.forward-15-symbolic) featuring crisp circular arrows with the number '15' in the center, built-in #fee14d golden yellow styling, GResource registration, and multi-tier embedded fallback. Reason: Ensures the 15-second skip controls render clearly, beautifully, and strictly in signature golden yellow under all desktop environments, themes, and Flatpak runtimes.</li>
          <li>Precision Audio Seeking &amp; Text Highlight Synchronization: Added relative seeking backend methods (seek(seconds_delta)) in Reader, BaseAudioPlayer, GStreamerAudioPlayer, and SoundDeviceAudioPlayer, with instant binary search highlight synchronization, boundary clamping, and pause_resume_mark adjustment in ReadAloudWindow. Reason: Ensures audio playback, word highlight position, and text marks remain sample-accurate and visually synchronized when jumping forward or backward in time.</li>
          <li>Quick Listener Interactive Pause &amp; Resume Controls: Added one-click pause and resume functionality to the floating Quick Listener bubble. Clicking the bubble while audio is playing immediately pauses playback; clicking it while paused resumes playback seamlessly from the exact character offset where it was paused. Reason: Eliminates the friction of switching windows, restoring minimized applications, or mouse navigation back to the main window just to pause or resume playback.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Context-Sensitive Right-Click Menu: Added real-time context menu item updates in the bubble's right-click popover ("Export Audio", "Pause Playback" when playing, "Resume Playback" when paused, "Rewind 15s", "Stop Playback", "Fast Forward 15s", and "Read Highlighted Text" when idle). Reason: Ensures secondary right-click options remain fully synchronized with the user's active listening workflow.</li>
          <li>Bi-Directional Playback State Synchronization: Added automated state dispatch from ReadAloudWindow (start_playback, toggle_pause, stop_playback, seek_playback) to ListenerBubbleWindow, reinforced with a state verification check in the bubble's periodic timer. Reason: Guarantees the floating listener widget accurately mirrors playback status even when playback is controlled via keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+P, Escape) or bottom toolbar buttons in the main window.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Universal Play/Pause Hover Expansion: Updated _on_motion_enter and _on_motion_move in ListenerBubbleWindow to trigger expansion when _current_playback_state in ("playing", "paused"), ensuring hovering over either the Play or Pause button reveals all controls. Reason: Restores user ability to view navigation and export options while paused without first resuming playback.</li>
          <li>Forced Highlight Update and Text Scrolling on Seek: Updated _update_highlight with a force parameter and clamped boundary selection, ensuring seeking immediately applies highlight tags and scrolls the text buffer into view even during paused states. Reason: Eliminates desynchronization between audio position and visible editor text when navigating.</li>
          <li>Euclidean 5-Zone Coordinate Routing: Updated _on_drag_end and pointer motion tracking to calculate Euclidean distance from cursor (x, y) to the 5 button centers in the 216×216px space (Top Export: 108, 36; Left Rewind: 36, 108; Center Pause/Play: 108, 108; Right Forward: 180, 108; Bottom Stop: 108, 180). Reason: Provides accurate, seamless hit detection and hover highlights across the circular cross layout while preserving drag repositioning when dragged greater than 8 pixels.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Tooltip &amp; Pointer Feedback: Updated Quick Listener tooltips and pointer hover states to dynamically report the active control underneath the pointer ("Export Audio (current tab or all tabs)", "Rewind 15 seconds", "Pause playback", "Resume playback", "Stop playback", "Fast forward 15 seconds", "Read highlighted text"). Reason: Delivers immediate, clear affordance to users on mouse hover regarding what clicking each portion of the widget will do.</li>
          <li>Automated Test Suite Expansion (117 Tests Passing): Added unit tests across tests/test_bubble.py and tests/test_pause_voice_switch.py verifying the 1.5s leave debounce delay, hover expansion when paused, and paused seek auto-resume. Reason: Guarantees high stability, complete code coverage, and automated regression prevention across all Quick Listener and audio seeking capabilities.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Flicker-Free 1.5s Debounced Hover Transitions: Quick Listener controls linger stably for 1.5 seconds upon pointer leave, preventing flickering when moving across buttons or brushing past the widget. Reason: Completely eliminates rapid blinking or jarring collapse animations during mouse interaction.</li>
          <li>216×216px Circular Cross Layout (.listener-bubble-box.expanded): Replaced horizontal capsule with a 216×216px circular container (border-radius: 50%) with a 3-row vertical box holding Export Audio at the top, a 3-column middle box for Rewind, Pause, and Forward, and Stop at the bottom. Reason: Replaces the elongated horizontal bar with an elegant, symmetrical circular controller that naturally fits all directional actions.</li>
          <li>Dead-Center Icon Alignment in Sub-Buttons: Centered all 5 icons horizontally and vertically within their respective 54×54px circular hit boxes (halign=CENTER, valign=CENTER, hexpand=True, vexpand=True). Reason: Eliminates visual off-center skewing where icons were previously aligned against the left or top edge of their container cells.</li>
          <li>Uniform Optical 32px Icon Sizing: Harmonized all 5 sub-button icons (Export CD, Rewind 15s, Pause/Play, Stop square, and Fast Forward 15s) to uniform 32px pixel size with matching visual weight and updated the Stop icon geometry to a 14×14 rounded square (rx=2.5). Reason: Resolves visual discrepancies where Pause was disproportionately large (45px) and Stop was tiny (16px), creating a cohesive, professional aesthetic.</li>
          <li>Complete Golden Yellow Icon Palette (#fee14d): Styled the Rewind, Pause, Play, Stop, and Forward icons in signature golden yellow (#fee14d) against the deep black circular background, while rendering the bundled Export Audio CD icon in crisp full fidelity. Reason: Establishes strong brand consistency with the ReadAloud megaphone application identity and ensures maximum legibility.</li>
          <li>Sub-Button Circular Hover Halos &amp; Tactile Bounce Animations: Added subtle translucent circular hover halos (rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18)) and click bounce scaling animations (.icon-bounce, scale(0.85)) on all sub-buttons. Reason: Gives immediate, polished tactile feedback when hovering and clicking buttons in the expanded cross layout.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Icon State Machine (Speaker ➔ Pause ➔ Play ➔ Speaker): The bubble center icon dynamically flips to a pause icon (media-playback-pause-symbolic) when playback starts, transitions to a play icon (media-playback-start-symbolic) when paused, and returns to the speaker app icon (im.zackarious.ReadAloud) when playback finishes or stop is clicked. Reason: Provides instantaneous visual indication of playback state directly on the desktop companion widget.</li>
          <li>3D Flip Transition Animation (.icon-flip): Maintained CSS 3D Y-axis rotation (rotateY(180deg)) and scaling transitions (scale(0.75)) when transitioning between speaker, pause, and play icons. Reason: Delivers an engaging, tactile visual flip effect that feels responsive and polished.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.6" date="2026-09-15">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.6 introduces dedicated Wayland window management integration for KDE Plasma 6 to automatically keep the Quick Listener bubble above other windows, resolves active-window focus conflicts when typing in the text editor, expands the floating Quick Listener bubble size by 25% with a mathematically circular profile, redesigns the bubble visual theme to a sleek high-contrast black fill with crisp white border and centered speaker icon with all outer shading removed, and increases default startup window height by 200px (700×700), supported by 97 automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Immediate Script Unlink in KWin Keep-Above Initialization: Removed immediate os.unlink() deletion of the temporary KWin ECMAScript file. Reason: In KDE Plasma 6 on Wayland, KWin parses and executes script files asynchronously; immediately unlinking the temporary file caused KWin 6's script engine to fail with a "Could not open script file" error, preventing automatic keep-above window rules from being registered.</li>
          <li>Global /Scripting start DBus Invocation on KDE Plasma 6: Removed calling the global /Scripting start DBus method. Reason: In KDE Plasma 6, /Scripting start is a legacy no-op when other scripts are already registered; executing run() directly on the loaded script object (/Scripting/Script{id}) guarantees script execution.</li>
          <li>Outer Drop-Shadow and Box Shading on Quick Listener: Removed the fuzzy outer box-shadow and blur shading surrounding the floating Quick Listener bubble (.listener-bubble-box). Reason: Eliminates visual noise and halo artifacts, producing a crisp, clean aesthetic that integrates seamlessly against light and dark desktop wallpapers alike.</li>
          <li>Fixed Pixel Border-Radius on Listener Bubble: Removed static pixel-based border rounding in favor of border-radius: 50%. Reason: Ensures the bubble remains a mathematically perfect circle regardless of container padding, scaling, or display DPI.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>KDE Plasma 6 / KWin Wayland Dedicated Script Object Runner: Added capture of the integer script ID from loadScript and direct execution of org.kde.kwin.Script.run() on DBus path /Scripting/Script{id}, guarded by isScriptLoaded() with a persistent /tmp/kwin_readaloud_keepabove.js script file. Reason: Guarantees that the floating Quick Listener automatically stays above all windows (including full-screen and maximized applications like Firefox) on KDE Plasma 6 Wayland without requiring the user to manually right-click and set "Keep above other windows".</li>
          <li>Active-Window Focus &amp; Selection Guard: Added an active-window check (main_window.is_active()) to the bubble's periodic keep-above timer to suppress present() while the main application window is active. Reason: Resolves an input conflict where typing or selecting text in the editor was unselected every two seconds by GTK window presentation calls.</li>
          <li>Mathematically Centered Speaker Icon: Added precise zero-margin center alignment rules for the megaphone speaker icon within the circular listener bubble container. Reason: Eliminates visual asymmetry and ensures the speaker icon sits perfectly dead-center within the circular bubble frame.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Extended Default Startup Window Height (+200px, 700×700): Updated default window dimensions in window.ui and recompiled readaloud.gresource to increase the initial startup window height from 500px to 700px. Reason: Provides an expansive, square 700×700 editing canvas for multi-paragraph reading and viewing upon application launch without vertical cramping.</li>
          <li>Automated Test Suite Expansion &amp; Validation (97 Tests Passing): Updated tests/test_bubble.py and tests/test_system_integrity.py to validate 72px bubble dimensions, 45px icon scaling, 50% border radius, 700px default window height, and active-window focus preservation during keep-above cycles. Reason: Guarantees high stability and automated regression prevention across all window managers and desktop environments.</li>
          <li>KWin DBus Keep-Above Script Logic: Updated the embedded KWin ECMAScript to monitor window addition events (workspace.windowAdded) and re-apply keepAbove = true dynamically to the ReadAloud floating listener. Reason: Ensures newly opened or fullscreen windows cannot eclipse the floating listener bubble during active desktop sessions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>25% Quick Listener Bubble Size Increase (72×72px): Enlarged the floating listener bubble diameter from 58px to 72px, paired with a proportionally scaled 45px megaphone speaker icon. Reason: Improves visual prominence and creates a larger, more accessible click and drag target on modern high-resolution displays.</li>
          <li>High-Contrast Monochrome Bubble Palette: Redesigned the Quick Listener bubble with a solid black background (#000000), a crisp 2px solid white border (#ffffff), and a pure white megaphone icon. Reason: Delivers striking visual contrast and high legibility across any desktop wallpaper or application window.</li>
          <li>True 50% Circular Bubble Profile: Applied border-radius: 50% to the bubble container. Reason: Replaces approximate rounded corners with a geometrically perfect circle.</li>
          <li>Enlarged 700×700 Main Document Window: Scaled the primary application window to 700×700 pixels on startup. Reason: Eliminates cramped vertical viewing space and allows users to read and edit substantial text without immediate scrolling.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.5" date="2026-09-08">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.5 introduces a full-featured tabbed document system, multi-tab batch audio export with live progress counters, window close audio export safeguards with tab-specific options, instant playback audio caching for unedited text, fixed per-model acoustic pitches across all 35 Piper neural voice models, active selection checkmarks in dropdown menus, and a modern rounded word highlight with 2x padding and 10px border radius, supported by automated unit tests.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pitch Control UI and Manual Adjustment Slider: Removed the pitch button, popup menu, and slider from the bottom toolbar. Reason: Each voice model has an optimal acoustic frequency; replacing manual pitch sliders with fixed, curated per-model pitches prevents voice distortion and eliminates clutter from the toolbar.</li>
          <li>Truncated Text in Dropdown Popup Menus: Removed character caps and ellipsis truncation from popup list items in both the voice model and language dropdowns. Reason: Ensures users can read complete model names, accents, and quality descriptions when choosing voices rather than truncated snippets.</li>
          <li>Hard-Edged Rectangular Word Highlighting: Removed the 0px radius, 0-padding rectangular background highlight on active words during playback. Reason: The harsh rectangular box crowded characters; replacing it with a 10px rounded pill with 2x padding produces a smoother, more legible reading experience.</li>
          <li>Flickering Modal Re-creation in Batch Audio Export: Removed destroying and re-instantiating the loading HUD dialog between sequential files during multi-tab audio export. Reason: Rapidly tearing down and creating modal dialogs caused severe visual screen flicker; preserving the HUD continuously ensures a smooth, non-disruptive export experience.</li>
          <li>Unprompted Window Closure on Exit: Removed immediate silent exit on window close when tabs contain unexported text content. Reason: Exiting without checking for unexported audio risked accidental data loss; prompting users with export choices safeguards synthesized audio work.</li>
          <li>Unhandled File Chooser Cancellation Errors: Removed unhandled GLib.GError exceptions when dismissing open and save text file dialogs. Reason: Dismissing or pressing Escape on file dialogs is normal user behavior; trapping cancellations cleanly prevents unhandled exception tracebacks in the terminal.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Standard Playback, Export &amp; Speed Keyboard Shortcuts: Added Ctrl + P to Play/Pause, Ctrl + E to Save Audio to file, Ctrl + Up to increase speaking speed by 0.1, and Ctrl + Down to decrease speaking speed by 0.1, with dedicated application action accelerators (win.play-audio, win.save-audio-as, win.speed-up, win.speed-down). Reason: Provides effortless, hands-on-keyboard control over core speech playback, speed adjustment, and audio saving workflows without needing mouse navigation.</li>
          <li>Hardened File Dialog &amp; I/O Error Handling: Added graceful exception handling across open and save dialog dismissals, missing/unreadable files with Latin-1 encoding fallback, and filesystem write errors with user-friendly error banners. Reason: Prevents unhandled Gio GError crashes when users dismiss file choosers or select unreadable/protected files.</li>
          <li>Playback Stop Precedence over Buffer Validation: Added immediate stop handling in the Read/Stop button handler so clicking Stop when text buffer is blank or cleared stops playback directly rather than popping up a "No text to read" error. Reason: Guarantees users can always reliably stop ongoing audio playback regardless of changes to the text buffer.</li>
          <li>Synthesized Audio Playback Caching &amp; Instant Replay: Added playback audio caching so stopping playback before completion and pressing Play again instantly replays the existing synthesized audio from the start without re-running Piper neural synthesis if text and speech parameters have not changed. Reason: Eliminates unnecessary synthesis wait times and CPU spikes when users pause, stop, and restart listening to unedited text.</li>
          <li>Batch Audio Export Progress Counter: Added live progress feedback in the speech generation loading HUD showing the active file index and total files count (e.g. "Generating file 1 of 30"). Reason: Eliminates guesswork during multi-file operations by informing users of exact batch progress and remaining file count.</li>
          <li>Window Close Audio Export Safeguard Dialog: Added confirmation dialog when clicking the Close button or pressing Ctrl + Q with unexported audio files, offering to export the current tab, export all tabs, close without exporting, or cancel. Reason: Prevents accidental loss of audio work upon exiting while allowing users to export single or multiple documents in one seamless flow.</li>
          <li>Per-Tab Audio Export State Tracking: Added intelligent export tracking per tab that monitors audio generation and marks tabs unexported if buffer text is modified. Reason: Avoids redundant export prompts for already saved or empty tabs while ensuring edited speech content is never lost.</li>
          <li>Document Tab System: Added full multi-tab document editing using AdwTabBar and AdwTabView with an inline add tab (+) button and Ctrl + T shortcut. Reason: Enables users to open, write, and manage multiple texts simultaneously without having to overwrite active documents.</li>
          <li>Tab Close Export Safeguard Dialog: Added confirmation dialog when closing tabs with unsaved content, offering to export audio, export text, close without exporting, or cancel. Reason: Protects user work from accidental closure while making speech and text export effortlessly accessible.</li>
          <li>Batch Multi-Tab Audio Export: Added prompt when clicking Save Audio with multiple open tabs to export all tabs or just the active tab. Reason: Allows users to export multi-chapter documents or notes into audio files in a single batch operation into a chosen folder.</li>
          <li>Fixed Pitch Presets for All 35 Piper Models: Added curated pitch settings for all 35 bundled Piper models (from 0.8 to 1.4) applied across playback, pause/resume, demos, and audio export. Reason: Automatically guarantees optimal voice fidelity for every model without requiring manual trial and error.</li>
          <li>Active Selection Checkmark in Language Dropdown: Added checkmark (✓) indicator next to the active language option in the popup list. Reason: Instantly confirms the currently selected language at a glance.</li>
          <li>Active Selection Checkmark in Voice Chooser Dropdown: Added checkmark (✓) indicator next to the active voice model in the popup list. Reason: Provides clear visual feedback of the active model selection across extensive voice lists.</li>
          <li>Floating Desktop Listener Bubble: Added a borderless, floating listener bubble window that launches automatically alongside ReadAloud and sits in the foreground. Clicking the bubble captures highlighted text selections from any application via the primary selection clipboard (with clipboard fallback), creates a new document tab in ReadAloud, and immediately starts audio playback with visual feedback. Reason: Provides effortless, one-click text-to-speech for text selected anywhere on the desktop across all applications without requiring manual copy-pasting.</li>
          <li>Expanded Automated Test Suite: Added comprehensive test coverage for the floating listener bubble, document tabs, batch audio export, audio caching, and application lifecycle management. Reason: Prevents regressions and guarantees robust behavior across multi-window and clipboard interactions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Batch Export Tab Audio Cache Assignment: Updated multi-tab batch audio export to assign each completed synthesis reader to its respective tab. Reason: Enables tabs exported in a batch to immediately replay audio without redundant re-synthesis if the user switches to them.</li>
          <li>Word Highlight Offset Type Validation: Updated playback position evaluation in highlight tracking to explicitly verify numeric types before boundary checks. Reason: Guards against potential TypeError runtime errors if non-numeric offsets are encountered.</li>
          <li>Standard Keyboard Shortcuts for File Actions (Ctrl + O, Ctrl + S): Added Ctrl + O for Open Text File and Ctrl + S for Save Text to File, registered standard action accelerators, and documented them in the Shortcuts Help Overlay. Reason: Conforms to standard desktop conventions and accelerates document editing workflows.</li>
          <li>Per-Tab Audio Cache Persistence on Tab Switch: Updated active tab navigation to preserve each document tab's synthesized audio reader and cleanly release temporary audio files on tab or window closure. Reason: Allows users to switch between open tabs and immediately replay audio without redundant synthesis, while preventing orphaned temporary files on disk.</li>
          <li>Version Date to 08 September 2026: Updated application release date to 08 September 2026 across UI, About window, and metainfo metadata. Reason: Reflects today's release with audio export progress indicators, window exit safeguards, and system integrity hardening.</li>
          <li>Reader Dialog Lifecycle Control (hide_dialog_on_complete): Updated Reader speech synthesis to accept hide_dialog_on_complete (default True, set False for batch exports). Reason: Gives callers explicit control over progress dialog persistence across sequential synthesis operations.</li>
          <li>Application Quit Action Routing (Ctrl + Q): Updated app.quit to route through active window close(). Reason: Guarantees keyboard shortcut exit triggers the unexported audio safeguard dialog identically to the title bar Close button.</li>
          <li>_setup_dropdown_excerpt() Dynamic Selection Tracking: Updated dropdown factory setup to support dynamic checkmark indicators with proper unbind signal disconnection (notify::selected). Reason: Maintains accurate selection states without leaking event handlers.</li>
          <li>Audio Playback Management on Tab Switch: Updated active tab change handler to automatically stop playback and clear highlight marks. Reason: Prevents audio desynchronization and ensures clean state transitions when navigating between documents.</li>
          <li>main_text_view Backward-Compatible Property: Updated main_text_view to dynamically return the active tab's text view. Reason: Seamlessly preserves compatibility with all existing methods and tests while supporting multi-tab architecture.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Keyboard Shortcuts Help Overlay (Playback &amp; File Groups): Added dedicated "Playback" group in the Shortcuts Help Overlay documenting Play/Pause (Ctrl + P / F5), Stop Playback (Escape), and Speed Adjustments (Ctrl + Up / Down), alongside Save Audio to File (Ctrl + E) in the File group. Reason: Makes speech control and audio saving keybindings transparently visible and discoverable within the application UI.</li>
          <li>Loading HUD Batch Progress Label (.batch-label): Added styled semi-bold label (105% font size, white text) in the translucent floating HUD displaying "Generating file X of Y". Reason: Delivers clear, prominent visual feedback of batch synthesis progress without crowding the time-remaining status label.</li>
          <li>Close Safeguard Dialog Response Styling: Styled "Close Without Exporting" with destructive red styling and "All Tabs" with suggested blue accent. Reason: Conforms to GNOME Human Interface Guidelines to prevent accidental data loss and visually emphasize the primary action.</li>
          <li>AdwTabBar Document Tabs: Added an elegant native tab bar with individual close buttons, titles, and an add tab button. Reason: Provides intuitive, native multi-document navigation adhering to GNOME Human Interface Guidelines.</li>
          <li>Streamlined Bottom Toolbar: Cleaned up the bottom toolbar layout following the removal of pitch controls. Reason: Gives language, voice, speed, and playback buttons balanced spacing and prominence.</li>
          <li>Dropdown Popup Selection Checkmarks: Rendered bold checkmarks (✓) next to active items in Language and Voice dropdown lists. Reason: Enhances usability by making the current selection immediately obvious.</li>
          <li>Modern 10px Rounded Word Highlight Pill: Replaced rectangular text background with a 10px border radius pill with 2x padding and black text foreground. Reason: Conforms to contemporary design standards and provides smooth visual tracking.</li>
          <li>Fixed New Tab Button Icon: Replaced missing tab-new-symbolic icon with standard list-add-symbolic (+). Reason: Fixes broken image placeholder on the tab bar across all platforms.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.4" date="2026-09-06">
      <description>
        <p>Version 1.4 — Public Release. All known stability regressions have been resolved, licensing and attribution documentation is now fully in-app, export workflows are streamlined with contextual file naming, button styling and dimensions have been unified across the window with borderless hover feedback, voice quality tiers and multi-speaker architecture are documented in the application description, and the interface is polished and regression-tested across 21 automated unit tests. ReadAloud is ready for open-source distribution.</p>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Solid Pill and Suggested-Action Styling on Bottom Buttons: Removed the permanent solid pill shape (pill class) and blue accent fill (suggested-action class) from the bottom-right playback and export controls. Reason: The heavy solid pill styling caused visual clutter and felt disconnected from the clean, flat style of the header controls; replacing them with flat action buttons creates an elegant, unified interface.</li>
          <li>Lined Border Outlines on Button Hover: Removed the 1px solid border outline from button hover and active states across the interface. Reason: The rigid border line felt distracting and dated; removing the border leaves a soft, modern translucent background highlight (alpha(currentColor, 0.10)) consistent with modern GNOME HIG.</li>
          <li>Generic Desktop Icons on Action Buttons: Removed generic system icons (document-open, document-save, and media-floppy-symbolic) from the top-left toolbar and export controls. Reason: Generic desktop icons lacked distinct visual identity, suffered from inconsistent scaling across themes, and did not clearly distinguish between saving text and exporting synthesized audio.</li>
          <li>Static &quot;audio.mp3&quot; Default Export Name: Removed the hardcoded static default filename &quot;audio.mp3&quot; from the audio export dialog. Reason: Required users to manually type descriptive file names each time; replacing it with an automated date-and-content title format ensures exported files are immediately identifiable and organized chronologically.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Voice Quality Levels &amp; Multi-Speaker Architecture in Application Description: Added comprehensive technical documentation explaining Piper's 4 voice quality tiers (x_low, low, medium, high with audio sample rates and parameter counts) and multi-speaker neural models directly inside the in-app Application Description sub-page and README. Reason: Educates users on the technical distinctions between bundled voices, helping them make informed choices regarding audio fidelity and multi-speaker trade-offs.</li>
          <li>Flaticon CD Audio Export Icon &amp; Full Legal Attribution: Added custom CD audio disc icon from Flaticon for the Save Audio button, with complete open-source attribution in the Licensing and Copyright Information page and interactive hyperlink in the Credits section. Reason: Clearly differentiates exporting audio from saving text files using an unmistakable media symbol, while fulfilling open-source licensing requirements.</li>
          <li>Megaphone Application Icon: Added vibrant new megaphone vector application icon and symbolic icon. Reason: Immediately conveys speech synthesis and vocal reading across desktop environments, docks, and application launchers.</li>
          <li>Contextual Audio Export Filename Generation: Added dynamic default export filenames formatted as &quot;[Day] [Month] [Year] - [First 5 Words].mp3&quot; (e.g. &quot;06 Sep 2026 - Hello World.mp3&quot;) with automatic sanitization of illegal filesystem characters and safe length limits. Reason: Automatically creates organized, readable, and chronologically sorted audio titles directly derived from the user's active text without requiring manual typing.</li>
          <li>Dedicated Licensing and Copyright Information Page: Added a dedicated &quot;Licensing and Copyright Information&quot; sub-page inside About ReadAloud. Reason: Provides transparent, legally accurate attribution for both the GPLv3 core application (ReadAloud as a fork of Parolu by wbernard), MIT-licensed Piper voice model files, Asam Munir UI icons (SVGRepo), and Flaticon CD icon, including full verbatim license texts and plain-English user rights summaries.</li>
          <li>Interactive Web Hyperlinks in Credits Sub-Page: Added clickable URL subtitle rows for all project authors, designers, voice repositories, and license sources in the About dialog's Credits section. Reason: Allows users to navigate directly to upstream projects, portfolios, and license terms with a single click.</li>
          <li>Voice Change Applied on Resume After Pause During Synthesis: Added support for correctly detecting and applying voice model changes when the user clicks Pause before synthesis has completed (i.e. before the GStreamer pipeline is created). Reason: A regression caused pause_audio() to return False when no pipeline existed yet, leaving is_paused = False. The fix introduces _is_paused and _stopped intent flags on Reader so pause intent is always recorded correctly regardless of synthesis state.</li>
          <li>Expanded Automated Unit Test Suite (21 Tests): Added regression tests covering export filename formatting and sanitization, legal attribution links, and credits page hyperlinks, bringing the automated test suite to 21 tests (21/21 passing). Reason: Guarantees high stability and automated regression prevention across all filename generation, playback, and documentation flows.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fine-Tuned 10% Icon Proportions for Visual Breathing Room: Reduced action icon sizes by 10% across the interface (top-left header icons scaled from 32px to 29px; bottom playback icons scaled from 28px to 25px; CD export icon scaled from 30px to 27px). Reason: Eliminates tight edge crowding inside button frames, giving icons well-balanced margins and comfortable visual breathing room.</li>
          <li>Standardized Button Dimensions (48px × 42px): Updated bottom-right playback and export buttons from wide 65px pills to 48px × 42px rectangles matching the top-left header buttons. Reason: Creates harmonious geometric consistency between top header controls and bottom toolbar controls across the entire window layout.</li>
          <li>SVGRepo Author Link in Legal Page: Updated the SVGRepo link to point directly to the Asam Munir author collection on SVGRepo. Reason: Provides accurate, specific attribution directly to the artist's repository collection.</li>
          <li>Custom Action Icons Standardized to 1:1 Square Canvas: Standardized action SVGs (folder-open, disk, and cd) to exact 1:1 square dimensions with zero exterior margins. Reason: Meets strict Flatpak and AppStream icon validation specifications while ensuring graphics scale up to fill button frames without unwanted margin shrinking.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Icon Size Preservation (_set_button_icon): Added a robust icon update method that maintains enlarged icon dimensions across dynamic button state transitions. Reason: Prevents GTK from resetting button icons to default 16px when toggling between Play, Pause, Resume, and Stop states.</li>
          <li>pause_audio() Pause Intent Tracking: Updated to set _is_paused = True and return True even when no GStreamer pipeline exists yet. Reason: Ensures window.is_paused is always set correctly when the user pauses during synthesis, enabling the voice-change-on-resume path to trigger reliably.</li>
          <li>resume_audio() Intent Clearing: Updated to clear _is_paused = False on resume. Reason: Prevents the pipeline from starting in the wrong PAUSED state if synthesis completes after the user has already resumed.</li>
          <li>_play_audio_file_async() Synthesis Guard and Pause-State Start: Updated to bail immediately if _stopped is set, and to start the GStreamer pipeline in PAUSED state when _is_paused is True. Reason: Prevents a replaced Reader from playing audio on behalf of an old voice, and honours pause intent during synthesis.</li>
          <li>stop_audio() Bus Signal Watch Cleanup: Updated to set _stopped = True, clear _is_paused, and remove the GStreamer bus signal watch before pipeline teardown. Reason: Eliminates ghost EOS callbacks that prematurely interrupted newly switched voices.</li>
          <li>_on_gst_message() Reader Identity Check: Updated EOS and error handlers to verify self.window.reader is self before calling window.stop_playback(). Reason: Prevents a replaced Reader's completion callback from stopping the new Reader's playback.</li>
          <li>GTK Thread-Safety Fix (set_sensitive): Updated set_sensitive(True) in the synthesis completion block to be dispatched via GLib.idle_add. Reason: Direct GTK widget operations from background threads violate GTK4's single-threaded model and can cause silent failures or deadlocks.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unified Transparent Action Buttons with Borderless Hover: Styled bottom-right playback and export buttons identically to the top-left header buttons, featuring transparent idle backgrounds and a smooth translucent background fill on hover without harsh border lines. Reason: Establishes visual harmony between top and bottom controls and conforms to modern GNOME HIG design patterns.</li>
          <li>10% Scaled Icon Dimensions (29px Header, 25px/27px Toolbar): Refined icon rendering sizes across all buttons. Reason: Delivers an aesthetically pleasing balance between icon prominence and button padding.</li>
          <li>Megaphone Application Icon: Replaced the application icon and symbolic icon with a vibrant megaphone graphic. Reason: Immediately conveys speech synthesis and vocal reading across desktop environments and application launchers.</li>
          <li>Dedicated CD Audio Export Icon: Replaced the floppy disk audio export icon with a dedicated CD audio disc icon from Flaticon. Reason: Differentiates saving audio recordings from saving text files with an unmistakable, intuitive media symbol.</li>
          <li>Custom Asam Munir Disk and Folder Icons: Replaced monochrome icons with custom yellow folder and green floppy disk vector designs. Reason: Greatly enhances visual clarity, charm, and immediate recognition of file operations.</li>
          <li>Aligned Header Button Heights (42px): Unified heights of Open, Save Text, and Test Demo Selector buttons to 42px. Reason: Maintains harmonious height and vertical alignment across the header bar.</li>
          <li>Voice Chooser Popup Full-Text Factory: Fixed _setup_dropdown_excerpt() to always create a dedicated full-text list factory for the voice chooser dropdown popup. Reason: Displays full, untruncated voice names in the popup list while keeping the closed button neatly abbreviated.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.3" date="2026-09-05">
      <description>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Standalone Starred Icon for Demos: Removed the generic star icon (starred-symbolic) on the header bar demo button. Reason: A generic star icon lacked immediate clarity for users; replacing it with an explicit text label &quot;Test Demo Selector&quot; instantly communicates its purpose and invites exploration.</li>
          <li>Ambiguous Model Variant Fallback: Removed ambiguous voice matching by voice prefix alone in speech synthesis and selection. Reason: When multiple quality variants of a voice exist (such as Low, Medium, and High), prefix matching caused lower-quality models to shadow higher-quality models; matching exact model IDs ensures the chosen quality variant is strictly honored.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Curated Preset Voice Demos (Demos 1, 2, 3): Added built-in preset voice demos showcasing different voices, languages, pitches, speeds, and historical texts: Demo 1: English (UK), Jenny Dioco Voice (en_GB-jenny_dioco-medium), pitch 1.3, speed 0.5 (William Wallace Betrayal). Demo 2: English (UK), Northern English Male (en_GB-northern_english_male-medium), pitch 1.3, speed 0.5 (Death of King Henry VIII). Demo 3: English (US), Joe Voice Medium Quality (en_US-joe-medium), pitch 1.2, speed 0.6 (Indigenous Peoples of the Americas). Reason: Enables users to instantly experience and test high quality Piper neural voice synthesis across varied accents and speech rates with one click.</li>
          <li>Overwrite Warning Protection Dialog: Added an Adw.AlertDialog confirmation prompt when selecting a demo with existing text in the input box. Reason: Prevents accidental loss of user-written text while allowing immediate one-click loading if the text box is empty.</li>
          <li>Automatic Demo Settings and Playback: Added automatic configuration of language, voice, pitch, speed, and immediate speech playback upon selecting a demo. Reason: Delivers an effortless, instant demo listening experience without requiring manual button clicks or control tweaking.</li>
          <li>Loading Window Visual Progress Bar: Added a modern progress bar (Gtk.ProgressBar) inside the speech generation HUD. Reason: Gives clear visual feedback on the exact percentage of speech synthesis completed rather than an indeterminate spinner alone.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Time Remaining Countdown: Added real-time calculation and display of remaining synthesis time (e.g. Generating audio: 45% (~3s remaining)). Reason: Informs the user of expected wait times during multi-sentence speech generation.</li>
          <li>Demo Menu Integration: Added a dedicated &quot;Test Demo Selector&quot; button in the header bar and a &quot;Preset Demos&quot; submenu in the hamburger menu. Reason: Ensures presets are highly accessible and discoverable from anywhere in the interface.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Version Number to 1.3: Updated application version by 0.1 to Version 1.3 with release date formatting across UI, Meson, metainfo, and documentation. Reason: Reflects the addition of preset demos, overwrite confirmation safety, loading progress bar with countdown, and header bar demo controls.</li>
          <li>Voice Selection by Exact Model ID: Updated voice chooser and reader communication to use full model IDs (e.g. en_US-joe-medium, en_US-ryan-high) instead of raw voice names. Reason: Accurately differentiates between different quality variants (Low, Medium, High) of the same voice.</li>
          <li>Demo 3 Voice Configuration: Updated Demo 3 from Ryan High Quality to Joe Voice Medium Quality (en_US-joe-medium) with pitch 1.2 and speed 0.6. Reason: User requested Joe voice preset for better demonstration of US English narration.</li>
          <li>Expanded Unit Test Suite: Added tests/test_demos.py covering demo presets, overwrite logic, auto-playback, model resolution, and wait dialog progress updates (10/10 tests passing). Reason: Guarantees high stability and automated regression detection across all new preset and loading features.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Header Bar &quot;Test Demo Selector&quot; Button: Replaced the icon-only star button with a prominent text label &quot;Test Demo Selector&quot;. Reason: Greatly increases UI clarity and discoverability on desktop displays.</li>
          <li>Sleek Loading HUD with Progress Bar and Countdown: Enhanced the translucent floating HUD with an Adw.Spinner, a rounded blue progress bar (Gtk.ProgressBar), and a typography-optimized status label. Reason: Upgrades speech generation from an opaque wait into a polished, modern, and informative visual indicator.</li>
          <li>Preset Submenu in Hamburger Menu: Added a structured &quot;Preset Demos&quot; section in the primary menu. Reason: Follows GNOME Human Interface Guidelines for secondary actions while keeping the header bar tidy.</li>
          <li>Change Log Window Sizing (+150px Width, 600×750): Increased default window width by an additional 150px (from 450×750 to 600×750) and scaled internal clamp limits to 650px. Reason: Provides a wider, more spacious reading canvas for release notes with longer line lengths, optimal paragraph margins, and reduced vertical scrolling.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.2" date="2026-09-05">
      <description>
        <p>Features and Fixes Removed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Static Playback Pipeline on Resume: Removed the static GStreamer pipeline resume behavior that unconditionally played pre-synthesized audio when unpausing. Reason: Prevented users from changing the voice model, language, pitch, or speed while playback was paused, as resuming merely unpaused the old audio stream.</li>
          <li>Single-Export Limitation and Coupled Pipeline: Removed monolithic speech synthesis pipeline that restricted saving audio to only once per session. Reason: Pipeline file locks and unreleased GStreamer bus resources caused subsequent exports to fail; decoupling synthesis from playback enables unlimited sequential saves.</li>
          <li>Stale Playback Audio Caching: Removed saving from playback cache. Reason: Editing text in the input box and clicking Save previously saved old audio from previous playback; dynamic synthesis ensures active text buffer is always exported.</li>
          <li>Uncompressed WAV as Default Format: Removed WAV as sole/default export format. Reason: WAV produces enormous uncompressed PCM files; voice notes and audiobooks require efficient, shareable formats.</li>
          <li>Intrusive Modal Loading Dialog: Removed heavy modal dialog with window borders, titlebar, and progress bar. Reason: Blocked user view and disrupted workflow during background synthesis.</li>
          <li>Overly Long Dropdown Labels: Removed full country names (&quot;English (United Kingdom)&quot; and &quot;English (United States)&quot;). Reason: Full names cluttered toolbar and crowded playback buttons.</li>
          <li>Unclipped Dropdown Button Text: Removed 76-character unclipped labels on closed toolbar dropdown buttons. Reason: Long voice descriptions stretched top toolbar and distorted window layout.</li>
          <li>Generic Document Save Icon: Removed generic document-save icon. Reason: Did not clearly convey immediate audio file export compared to classic disk symbol.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Added:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Dynamic Mid-Stream Voice Switching on Resume: Added ability to switch voice model, language, pitch, or speed while paused, seamlessly re-synthesizing and resuming playback from the paused word using the newly selected voice. Reason: Resolves the bug where changing voice models during pause had no effect when resuming playback.</li>
          <li>Text-Anchored Position Tracking (pause_resume_mark): Added Gtk.TextMark anchoring to the exact character offset of the paused word. Reason: Guarantees playback resumes accurately at the right word even if text before or after the paused word is edited while paused.</li>
          <li>Keyboard Playback Shortcuts (F5 and Escape): Added F5 to toggle Play/Pause and Escape to stop playback. Reason: Provides immediate hands-on-keyboard audio control without requiring mouse interaction.</li>
          <li>Voice-Optimized MP3 Export (64 kbps Mono): Added native GStreamer MP3 encoding with descriptive format options. Reason: Delivers clear spoken-word audio with ~95% file size reduction, ideal for voice notes, podcasts, and portable listening.</li>
          <li>Descriptive Quality Explanations in Save Dialog: Added explicit format explanations in file chooser dialog (&quot;MP3 Audio — 64 kbps Mono, Voice/Podcast Optimized (*.mp3)&quot; and &quot;WAV Audio — Lossless Uncompressed PCM (*.wav)&quot;). Reason: Helps users make informed decisions about format and file size tradeoffs without technical confusion.</li>
          <li>Audio Playback Controls (Pause and Resume): Added dedicated Pause and Resume controls for speech playback. Reason: Allows users to pause and resume listening without losing text position.</li>
          <li>Real-Time Word Highlighting: Added synchronized yellow word-by-word highlighting with automatic view scrolling. Reason: Provides a clear visual tracking aid following speech progression in real time.</li>
          <li>Read from Cursor or Selection: Added synthesis starting cleanly from active cursor position or highlighted text. Reason: Allows users to listen to specific paragraphs or resume reading without starting from beginning.</li>
          <li>Dynamic Text Zoom: Added font scaling (70% to 300%) via Ctrl +, Ctrl -, Ctrl 0, and Ctrl + Mouse Scroll Wheel. Reason: Improves reading comfort and accessibility across different display sizes.</li>
          <li>Dedicated Change Logs Page: Added native Change Logs subpage inside About ReadAloud and direct menu action. Reason: Provides transparent, structured release notes and feature history in the app.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Features and Fixes Updated:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Version Number to 1.2: Updated application version to 1.2 with release date formatting across UI and metadata. Reason: Signals resolution of the voice switching resume bug, addition of text-anchored playback resume, and keyboard shortcut additions.</li>
          <li>Language Dropdown Options: Updated dropdown labels to &quot;English (UK)&quot; and &quot;English (US)&quot; with automatic migration for existing settings. Reason: Standardizes abbreviations while seamlessly preserving saved user preferences.</li>
          <li>Model Discovery Scanner: Updated directory scanning to safely handle read-only environments and support local development models. Reason: Prevents startup failures in sandboxed systems and simplifies testing.</li>
          <li>Automated Validation and Unit Testing Suite: Added unit tests (tests/test_pause_voice_switch.py) and integrated AppStream CLI validation into Meson tests. Reason: Ensures continuous regression prevention for voice switching, desktop entries, and AppStream compliance.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Visual Changes and UI Updates:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Save Button Disk Icon: Replaced document-save icon with classic floppy disk icon (media-floppy-symbolic). Reason: The floppy disk is the universally recognized symbol for quick save actions.</li>
          <li>Dropdown 40-Character Excerpt: Configured closed dropdown buttons to display a 40-character excerpt with ellipsis and tooltip, while preserving full text in dropdown menu. Reason: Keeps toolbar buttons neatly proportioned while allowing users to read complete descriptions.</li>
          <li>Immediate Resume Word Highlight: Configured the paused word to highlight immediately when resuming with a new voice. Reason: Provides visual continuity showing users exactly where the newly selected voice will start reading.</li>
          <li>Change Log Window Sizing (+25% Dimensions): Increased default window dimensions by 25% (from 360×600 to 450×750) and scaled internal clamp limits. Reason: Provides a more spacious reading area for documentation with less scrolling and improved line readability.</li>
          <li>Modern Transparent Loading HUD: Replaced old dialog with borderless, floating on-screen HUD with translucent frosted glass styling and AdwSpinner. Reason: Creates a sleek, non-intrusive visual indicator during speech generation.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
